0
00:00:09,414 --> 00:00:11,983
MY MAMA THINKS I WAS BORN
TO BE A TOP MODEL.

1
00:00:13,518 --> 00:00:16,321
AND SOMEHOW,
I GOT FROM THIS...

2
00:00:18,390 --> 00:00:21,059
TO THIS.

3
00:00:21,059 --> 00:00:23,328
ARE TOP MODELS
BORN OR MADE?

4
00:00:24,996 --> 00:00:27,632
YOU'RE NOT BORN A TOP MODEL,
I CAN TELL YOU THAT.

5
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:30,368
YOU HAVE TO WORK FOR IT.

6
00:00:33,972 --> 00:00:36,641
OUR LAST THREE WINNERS
STUDIED, STRUGGLED...

7
00:00:36,641 --> 00:00:38,043
I'M NOT FINISHED!

8
00:00:38,043 --> 00:00:39,511
AND WENT ALL OUT...

9
00:00:39,511 --> 00:00:41,446
- EVA.
- (squealing)

10
00:00:41,446 --> 00:00:44,116
TO ACHIEVE THEIR DREAMS.

11
00:00:44,116 --> 00:00:45,984
NOW THOUSANDS MORE
SENT ME THEIR TAPES,

12
00:00:45,984 --> 00:00:48,320
HOPING I MIGHT SEE THEIR
TOP MODEL POTENTIAL.

13
00:00:50,055 --> 00:00:52,791
WHO WILL GO FROM
AN UNKNOWN TO A TOP MODEL?

14
00:00:52,791 --> 00:00:56,328
THESE GIRLS BETTER WORK IT,
STARTING RIGHT NOW!

15
00:01:02,601 --> 00:01:07,472
MY NAME'S NOELLE,
AND I'M WAY EXCITED.

16
00:01:07,472 --> 00:01:10,108
I AM READY TO COMPETE AGAINST
THE MOST GORGEOUS GIRLS

17
00:01:10,108 --> 00:01:12,144
I'LL PROBABLY
EVER SEE IN MY LIFE.

18
00:01:12,744 --> 00:01:15,247
I'M KAHLEN,
AND I JUST LANDED IN L.A.

19
00:01:15,247 --> 00:01:17,249
IT'S A LITTLE WEIRD.
I NEVER BEEN HERE BEFORE.

20
00:01:17,249 --> 00:01:19,284
I'M A SMALL TOWN GIRL,
SO THIS IS CRAZY.

21
00:01:19,284 --> 00:01:21,987
♪♪♪

22
00:01:21,987 --> 00:01:24,823
MY NAME IS BRITTANY, AND
I'M FROM TALLAHASSEE, FLORIDA.

23
00:01:24,823 --> 00:01:27,192
THIS IS WHAT I WANTED DO
SINCE DAY ONE OF MY LIFE.

24
00:01:27,192 --> 00:01:29,361
WHATEVER IT TAKES TO WIN,
BABY! I'M IN!

25
00:01:30,529 --> 00:01:32,164
I'M BRANDY.

26
00:01:32,164 --> 00:01:33,965
THIS IS MY FIRST TIME
RIDIN' A PLANE.

27
00:01:33,965 --> 00:01:36,802
THIS IS JUST, LIKE,
TOTALLY TRIPPING ME OUT.

28
00:01:36,802 --> 00:01:38,336
- LLUVY.
- LLUVY? KAHLEN.

29
00:01:38,336 --> 00:01:40,705
I'M LLUVY, AND I WAS
BORN IN MEXICO.

30
00:01:40,705 --> 00:01:43,141
NOW I'M JUST
A CALIFORNIA GIRL.

31
00:01:45,677 --> 00:01:47,212
MY NAME IS TIFFANY.

32
00:01:47,212 --> 00:01:48,413
I'M FROM MIAMI, FLORIDA.

33
00:01:48,413 --> 00:01:51,550
AND I AM SO EXCITED TO BE
HERE FOR A SECOND CHANCE.

34
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:52,984
WHAT'S UP?

35
00:01:52,984 --> 00:01:55,921
FIRST TIME I CAME HERE,
AND I GOT IN A FIGHT.

36
00:01:55,921 --> 00:01:58,023
(screaming)

37
00:02:00,725 --> 00:02:03,795
THAT STANK HO
POURED A BEER ON MY WEAVE!

38
00:02:06,331 --> 00:02:07,332
I CAME BACK--

39
00:02:07,332 --> 00:02:08,800
I AM NOT GOING TO SAY
A DIFFERENT PERSON--

40
00:02:08,800 --> 00:02:11,937
BUT IN A LOT OF WAYS
I'M A BETTER PERSON.

41
00:02:11,937 --> 00:02:14,439
I KNOW I HAVE TO DO GOOD
THIS TIME.

42
00:02:14,439 --> 00:02:16,508
♪♪♪

43
00:02:30,188 --> 00:02:32,390
I AUDITIONED
FOR THE LAST COMPETITION,

44
00:02:32,390 --> 00:02:34,392
AND I DIDN'T MAKE IT.

45
00:02:34,392 --> 00:02:36,428
- TOCCARA.
- WHOO!

46
00:02:37,562 --> 00:02:39,331
IT RIPPED MY HEART OUT.

47
00:02:39,331 --> 00:02:41,032
I TRIED OUT AGAIN.

48
00:02:41,032 --> 00:02:42,601
THIS IS MY SECOND CHANCE,

49
00:02:42,601 --> 00:02:44,936
AND I AM NOT WASTING
ANYTHING WITH THIS ONE.

50
00:02:44,936 --> 00:02:47,706
♪♪♪

51
00:02:47,706 --> 00:02:50,275
THE FIRST TIME I SAW
EVERYONE ALL TOGETHER

52
00:02:50,275 --> 00:02:53,478
WAS WHEN WE ALL MET
IN A BIG ROOM,

53
00:02:53,478 --> 00:02:54,980
AND EVERYONE WAS KINDA
CHECKING EACH OTHER OUT

54
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:57,749
AND TRYING TO FIGURE OUT
WHO'S THEIR COMPETITION.

55
00:02:57,749 --> 00:02:58,984
HELLO.

56
00:02:58,984 --> 00:03:02,454
- (screaming)
- (applause)

57
00:03:02,454 --> 00:03:03,855
SO WELCOME TO L.A.

58
00:03:03,855 --> 00:03:06,992
AND WELCOME TO THE WESTIN
CENTURY PLAZA HOTEL.

59
00:03:08,126 --> 00:03:09,294
TAKE A LOOK
AROUND THIS ROOM.

60
00:03:09,294 --> 00:03:13,398
SOMEONE HERE IS AMERICA'S
NEXT TOP MODEL.

61
00:03:13,398 --> 00:03:15,100
(applause)

62
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:17,669
YOU GUYS BETTER GET YOUR
GAME ON AND BRING IT, OKAY?

63
00:03:17,669 --> 00:03:19,804
GET A SPACE IN THIS HOUSE.

64
00:03:19,804 --> 00:03:22,173
SO WHAT DO YOU THINK
TYRA IS LOOKING FOR?

65
00:03:22,173 --> 00:03:24,175
I THINK SHE IS LOOKING
FOR SOMEONE REALLY UNIQUE.

66
00:03:24,175 --> 00:03:25,510
SOMEBODY THAT'S REAL.

67
00:03:25,510 --> 00:03:26,845
SOMEBODY THAT CAN
BRING SOMETHING NEW.

68
00:03:26,845 --> 00:03:28,546
I THINK SHE'S LOOKING
FOR ME.

69
00:03:28,546 --> 00:03:31,082
- OH, ALL RIGHT.
- I KNOW WHAT I AM LOOKING FOR.

70
00:03:31,082 --> 00:03:33,018
- (screaming)
- (applause)

71
00:03:33,018 --> 00:03:35,921
♪♪♪

72
00:03:41,793 --> 00:03:44,462
I SAW EVERY SINGLE GIRL'S
TAPE IN HERE.

73
00:03:44,462 --> 00:03:45,997
I REMEMBER
THERE IS A GIRL IN HERE

74
00:03:45,997 --> 00:03:48,466
WHO FEELS LIKE SHE
ONCE WAS A CAT

75
00:03:48,466 --> 00:03:51,469
AND IS NOW
REINCARNATED AS A WOMAN.

76
00:03:51,469 --> 00:03:52,904
- RAWR.
- THIS IS HER.

77
00:03:52,904 --> 00:03:55,440
ISN'T YOUR NICKNAME LADY KAT
OR SOMETHING LIKE THAT?

78
00:03:55,440 --> 00:03:58,143
OH, MY GOSH!

79
00:03:58,143 --> 00:04:00,312
I AM LOOKING FOR GIRLS
WITH PIZZAZZ.

80
00:04:00,312 --> 00:04:02,647
I AM LOOKING FOR GIRLS THAT
ARE BEAUTIFUL ON THE OUTSIDE,

81
00:04:02,647 --> 00:04:04,582
BUT, DUH, MOST MODELS ARE
BEAUTIFUL ON THE OUTSIDE.

82
00:04:04,582 --> 00:04:06,751
BUT I AM LOOKING FOR
THE BEAUTY ON THE INSIDE.

83
00:04:06,751 --> 00:04:07,819
SOMETHING THAT IS RARE,

84
00:04:07,819 --> 00:04:09,688
SOMETHING
THAT IS EXTRA SPECIAL.

85
00:04:09,688 --> 00:04:11,923
JUST BE ON BUT BE YOURSELVES.
DON'T FAKE IT.

86
00:04:11,923 --> 00:04:13,825
I CAN SEE THROUGH
THE FAKE, OKAY?

87
00:04:13,825 --> 00:04:15,427
SO JUST BE REAL.

88
00:04:15,427 --> 00:04:17,829
- BYE-BYE.
- (screaming)

89
00:04:17,829 --> 00:04:20,231
SHE REALLY CARED.
SHE CAME.

90
00:04:20,231 --> 00:04:21,933
IT TOTALLY
PUMPED US UP FOR THE WEEK.

91
00:04:21,933 --> 00:04:24,869
♪♪♪

92
00:04:24,869 --> 00:04:26,538
WITH SO MANY GIRLS
TO CHOOSE FROM,

93
00:04:26,538 --> 00:04:29,908
I'M RELYING ON THE HELP OF MY
VERY OPINIONATED COLLEAGUES.

94
00:04:29,908 --> 00:04:32,677
MR. JAY MANUAL,
THE CREATIVE DIRECTOR

95
00:04:32,677 --> 00:04:34,212
OF ALL OF OUR PHOTO SHOOTS.

96
00:04:34,212 --> 00:04:35,413
I LOVE WHERE IT'S GOING,

97
00:04:35,413 --> 00:04:37,816
BUT IT'S LOOKING
A LITTLE HOOTCHIE.

98
00:04:37,816 --> 00:04:39,584
AND MISS J. ALEXANDER...

99
00:04:39,584 --> 00:04:40,852
POSTURE. BALANCE.

100
00:04:40,852 --> 00:04:44,089
OUR RUNWAY COACH
AND DIVA EXTRAORDINAIRE.

101
00:04:44,089 --> 00:04:45,991
IT'S ABOUT TO FALL, BUT
YOU'RE NOT LETTING IT HAPPEN.

102
00:04:45,991 --> 00:04:48,727
- IT'S NOT GONNA FALL.
- OH, OH!

103
00:04:50,061 --> 00:04:51,396
COME ON IN, REBECCA.

104
00:04:51,396 --> 00:04:52,597
MY NAME IS REBECCA.

105
00:04:52,597 --> 00:04:55,700
I'M 21, AND I'M FROM
MINNEAPOLIS, MINNESOTA.

106
00:04:55,700 --> 00:04:56,935
I LOVE THIS GIRL
SO MUCH.

107
00:04:56,935 --> 00:04:59,170
I AM ACTUALLY
ON MY WAY TO BEING MARRIED

108
00:04:59,170 --> 00:05:00,171
AND HAVING THE KIDS.

109
00:05:00,171 --> 00:05:02,907
BUT BEFORE I DO THAT,
I WANT TO HAVE FUN.

110
00:05:02,907 --> 00:05:05,677
YOU HAVE A VERY ALL-AMERICAN,
SLIGHTLY CALIFORNIA LOOK.

111
00:05:05,677 --> 00:05:08,113
HOW DO YOU SEE YOURSELF
BEING ABLE TO TRANSFORM?

112
00:05:08,113 --> 00:05:09,781
SWEET INNOCENCE IS
KIND OF MY COVER UP,

113
00:05:09,781 --> 00:05:12,283
AND I CAN DO SOME THINGS
AND STILL GET AWAY WITH IT.

114
00:05:12,283 --> 00:05:13,318
(gasps)

115
00:05:13,318 --> 00:05:15,120
I HAVE LIED AND CHEATED

116
00:05:15,120 --> 00:05:17,122
AND, YOU KNOW,
GOTTEN MY WAY.

117
00:05:17,122 --> 00:05:19,324
BUT I WANT PEOPLE TO SEE ME

118
00:05:19,324 --> 00:05:21,726
AS A GOOD, SWEET,
INNOCENT PERSON

119
00:05:21,726 --> 00:05:23,728
BECAUSE IT'S ALWAYS
WORKED IN MY FAVOR.

120
00:05:25,897 --> 00:05:27,365
I WAS VERY IMPRESSED
WITH HER.

121
00:05:27,365 --> 00:05:29,968
LIKE SHE WAS A VERY SWEET GIRL,
BUT SHE'S GOT SOME GRIT.

122
00:05:29,968 --> 00:05:32,137
- HI, EVERYBODY.
- HI.

123
00:05:32,137 --> 00:05:33,438
MY NAME IS KEENYAH.

124
00:05:33,438 --> 00:05:34,572
I AM STUDYING BIOLOGY

125
00:05:34,572 --> 00:05:36,641
AT THE UNIVERSITY
OF CALIFORNIA, RIVERSIDE.

126
00:05:36,641 --> 00:05:38,309
OKAY, WELL,
THIS IS MY STREET.

127
00:05:38,309 --> 00:05:41,446
I LIVE WITH MY FAMILY DURING
THE SUMMERTIME IN COMPTON.

128
00:05:42,981 --> 00:05:44,749
THE MEDIA
REPRESENTS COMPTON

129
00:05:44,749 --> 00:05:47,552
TO BE THIS PLACE WHERE YOU
WALK OUTSIDE, YOU GET SHOT.

130
00:05:47,552 --> 00:05:49,587
SO IF SOMEBODY WERE
TO SEE ME ANYWHERE

131
00:05:49,587 --> 00:05:50,722
AND SAY, "OH,
SHE'S FROM COMPTON?

132
00:05:50,722 --> 00:05:53,124
OH, I DIDN'T KNOW THAT THIS
CAN COME FROM COMPTON."

133
00:05:53,124 --> 00:05:55,126
BUT REMEMBER,
YOU REPRESENT YOU.

134
00:05:55,126 --> 00:05:57,028
YOU CAN INSPIRE PEOPLE

135
00:05:57,028 --> 00:05:58,596
AND SAY THAT YOU CAME
FROM THERE,

136
00:05:58,596 --> 00:06:00,031
BUT YOU WILL
REPRESENT WHO YOU ARE.

137
00:06:00,031 --> 00:06:01,733
- SO REMEMBER THAT.
- RIGHT.

138
00:06:01,733 --> 00:06:04,602
IF IT CAME BETWEEN MODELING
AND BEING A DOCTOR,

139
00:06:04,602 --> 00:06:07,238
I WOULD ABSOLUTELY
CHOOSE MODELING.

140
00:06:07,238 --> 00:06:08,807
THE WAY YOU CAN
REPRESENT YOURSELF

141
00:06:08,807 --> 00:06:11,910
WITHOUT SAYING A WORD,
I THINK THAT IS SO EXCELLENT.

142
00:06:11,910 --> 00:06:13,978
HEY, Y'ALL.
I'M KAHLEN.

143
00:06:13,978 --> 00:06:15,680
I'M FROM BROKEN ARROW,
OKLAHOMA.

144
00:06:15,680 --> 00:06:18,316
YOU'VE NEVER SEEN
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"?

145
00:06:18,316 --> 00:06:20,952
NO, I DON'T WATCH
A LOT OF TV.

146
00:06:20,952 --> 00:06:22,654
WE ONLY HAVE,
LIKE, THREE CHANNELS,

147
00:06:22,654 --> 00:06:24,589
AND I WORK 50 HOURS
A WEEK.

148
00:06:24,589 --> 00:06:26,724
I DON'T KNOW MUCH
ABOUT THE FASHION

149
00:06:26,724 --> 00:06:29,127
AND HOW TO WALK
OR HOW TO POSE FOR PICTURES.

150
00:06:29,127 --> 00:06:30,795
I WAS'NT SURE IF I COULD
ACTUALLY DO IT.

151
00:06:30,795 --> 00:06:32,130
WALK TOWARD US AND BACK.

152
00:06:34,966 --> 00:06:36,501
MM. MM-HMM.

153
00:06:40,071 --> 00:06:41,639
THANK YOU, KAHLEN.

154
00:06:44,442 --> 00:06:46,978
SHE'S WATCHING EVERY EPISODE
OF "AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL."

155
00:06:46,978 --> 00:06:48,113
- WITH THAT WALK.
- YOU KNOW WHAT?

156
00:06:48,113 --> 00:06:49,447
THAT WAS CARMEN CASS.

157
00:06:49,447 --> 00:06:50,715
AND THAT WAS WIND
IN YOUR HAIR.

158
00:06:50,715 --> 00:06:52,083
WE LIKE.

159
00:06:52,083 --> 00:06:54,953
MY NAME IS LINDSEY, I'M FROM
BATON ROUGE, LOUISIANA,

160
00:06:54,953 --> 00:06:55,954
AND I AM 21.

161
00:06:55,954 --> 00:06:57,122
MY FAMILY WAS MORMON.

162
00:06:57,122 --> 00:06:59,858
BIG MORMON FAMILY,
VERY CLOSE KNIT.

163
00:06:59,858 --> 00:07:02,594
BUT I DON'T BELIEVE IN GOD
AT THIS POINT IN MY LIFE.

164
00:07:02,594 --> 00:07:04,863
I TOLD MY MOTHER
THAT I WAS ATHEIST,

165
00:07:04,863 --> 00:07:07,398
AND SHE SAID THAT SHE WOULD
RATHER HAVE HEARD

166
00:07:07,398 --> 00:07:09,033
THAT I WAS
PREGNANT OR A LESBIAN.

167
00:07:09,033 --> 00:07:13,104
WELL, I AM FLABBERGASTED.

168
00:07:13,104 --> 00:07:16,808
AFTER PARTING WAYS
WITH THE MORMON RELIGION,

169
00:07:16,808 --> 00:07:19,377
I DID CHANGE THE WAY
THAT I SAW MYSELF.

170
00:07:19,377 --> 00:07:21,379
I KIND OF STARTED TO GO OUT
A LITTLE BIT MORE,

171
00:07:21,379 --> 00:07:24,282
STARTED TO CARE A LITTLE BIT
MORE ABOUT HAIR AND MAKEUP.

172
00:07:24,282 --> 00:07:26,084
- THANK YOU.
- THANK YOU.

173
00:07:26,084 --> 00:07:27,952
LOVE THE LEGS,
LOVE THE STRUT,

174
00:07:27,952 --> 00:07:28,987
NEEDS A HAIR CUT.

175
00:07:28,987 --> 00:07:30,989
HER HAIR LOOKS LIKE A WIG

176
00:07:30,989 --> 00:07:32,957
THAT YOU BOUGHT IN A STORE
FOR $19.99,

177
00:07:32,957 --> 00:07:34,125
AND IT'S CALLED A NANCY.

178
00:07:34,125 --> 00:07:36,127
YOU KNOW HOW THEY ALL
GOT A NAME? HER WIG--

179
00:07:36,127 --> 00:07:37,729
YOU KNOW THERE'S
A TYRA WIG OUT THERE.

180
00:07:37,729 --> 00:07:39,998
SHE SHOULD HAVE GONE
AND BOUGHT THE TYRA.

181
00:07:39,998 --> 00:07:42,133
- HI.
- YOUR FOREHEAD IS GORGEOUS.

182
00:07:42,133 --> 00:07:44,135
MY SISTER
WITH A BIG FOREHEAD.

183
00:07:44,135 --> 00:07:45,303
- I KNOW.
- WE LOVE THAT.

184
00:07:45,303 --> 00:07:48,907
MY NAME IS JENNIFER AND I'M
FROM RICHMOND, CALIFORNIA.

185
00:07:48,907 --> 00:07:49,908
WHEN I WAS YOUNGER,

186
00:07:49,908 --> 00:07:52,443
I REALLY DIDN'T HAVE
A LOT OF SELF-CONFIDENCE.

187
00:07:52,443 --> 00:07:55,580
BUT OVER THE YEARS,
I REALLY FOUND

188
00:07:55,580 --> 00:07:57,682
A PERSONAL
RELATIONSHIP WITH GOD,

189
00:07:57,682 --> 00:08:01,186
AND THAT'S MADE ME
A VERY STRONG PERSON.

190
00:08:01,186 --> 00:08:03,087
IF YOU BELIEVE IN SOMETHING,
AND ESPECIALLY

191
00:08:03,087 --> 00:08:06,057
IF YOU BELIEVE IN YOURSELF,
YOU CAN BE ANYTHING.

192
00:08:06,057 --> 00:08:08,693
HELLO.

193
00:08:08,693 --> 00:08:11,496
HOW ARE ALL YOU
FABULOUS PEOPLE DOING TODAY?

194
00:08:11,496 --> 00:08:14,499
'CAUSE I KNOW I AM DOING
VERY WELL, THANK YOU.

195
00:08:14,499 --> 00:08:16,534
I AM BRITTANY.
I AM 22 YEARS OLD.

196
00:08:16,534 --> 00:08:18,770
- HI.
- DID YOU HAVE RED BULL
THIS MORNING?

197
00:08:18,770 --> 00:08:20,171
NO, I AM ALWAYS
LIKE THIS.

198
00:08:20,171 --> 00:08:21,573
I'M LIKE, WHOO!

199
00:08:21,573 --> 00:08:23,341
- I AIN'T MAD AT YOU.
- DING, DING, DING.

200
00:08:23,341 --> 00:08:24,609
I'M A WINNER.

201
00:08:24,609 --> 00:08:26,878
I LOVE BEING OUTGOING,
I'M EXTREMELY OUTSPOKEN,

202
00:08:26,878 --> 00:08:28,479
I WANT TO BE THE CENTER
OF ATTENTION.

203
00:08:28,479 --> 00:08:31,382
I NEED TO ENTERTAIN.

204
00:08:31,382 --> 00:08:33,618
I'VE MUST HAVE BEEN
A DRAG QUEEN IN A FORMER LIFE.

205
00:08:33,618 --> 00:08:35,486
I LOVE BIG HAIR.
I'M ALL ABOUT SOME BIG HAIR.

206
00:08:35,486 --> 00:08:37,355
WOW. MAYBE I WILL GET
A SEX CHANGE

207
00:08:37,355 --> 00:08:38,789
SO I CAN BE A DUDE
SO I CAN DO DRAG.

208
00:08:38,789 --> 00:08:40,291
I ALREADY HAVE THE VOICE.

209
00:08:40,291 --> 00:08:43,094
HELLO, I AM MANLY STANLEY.

210
00:08:43,094 --> 00:08:45,495
THANK YOU.

211
00:08:45,495 --> 00:08:49,133
I WOULD LOVE TO PUT HER
AND JANICE IN A ROOM TOGETHER

212
00:08:49,133 --> 00:08:50,802
AND JUST SHUT THE DOOR.

213
00:08:50,802 --> 00:08:53,104
I THINK BRITTANY
MIGHT COME OUT ALIVE.

214
00:08:55,373 --> 00:08:58,209
- SOMEBODY'S BACK.
- HEY. I'M BACK.

215
00:08:58,209 --> 00:09:00,011
I'M TIFFANY.
I'M FROM MIAMI, FLORIDA,

216
00:09:00,011 --> 00:09:01,179
AND I'M 21 YEARS OLD.

217
00:09:01,179 --> 00:09:04,382
LAST TIME I CAME HERE
I TRIED OUT,

218
00:09:04,382 --> 00:09:06,050
I DIDN'T GET IN.

219
00:09:06,050 --> 00:09:07,452
IT WOULD HAVE BEEN
A BIG CHANGE

220
00:09:07,452 --> 00:09:11,256
FROM HUSTLING TO BEIN'
A GLAMOUR GIRL ANYWAY.

221
00:09:11,256 --> 00:09:13,291
IT'S COOL. YOU KNOW,
I'M USED TO FAILING.

222
00:09:13,291 --> 00:09:14,792
SOMEBODY GOT TO FAIL, RIGHT?

223
00:09:14,792 --> 00:09:16,094
THE LAST TIME I WAS HERE,

224
00:09:16,094 --> 00:09:19,063
I KNEW I HAD TO BE
CHANGING MY LIFE.

225
00:09:19,063 --> 00:09:20,765
I DON'T JUMP ON PEOPLE
AND THROW GLASSES

226
00:09:20,765 --> 00:09:22,367
AND STUFF LIKE THAT ANYMORE.

227
00:09:25,670 --> 00:09:28,139
I'M JUST NOT LIKE THAT
ANYMORE, I'M JUST NOT,

228
00:09:28,139 --> 00:09:30,041
AND I'M GLAD I'M NOT.

229
00:09:30,041 --> 00:09:32,677
I WENT BACK HOME AND I WENT
TO MY ANGER MANAGEMENT CLASS.

230
00:09:32,677 --> 00:09:33,711
THAT HELPED A LOT.

231
00:09:33,711 --> 00:09:35,280
EVERYTHING IN MY LIFE
IS HAPPY.

232
00:09:35,280 --> 00:09:37,582
I HAVE A LOT OF HELP
WITH MY BABY NOW,

233
00:09:37,582 --> 00:09:39,984
MY BOYFRIEND IS WONDERFUL.
HE'S GREAT.

234
00:09:39,984 --> 00:09:41,753
I'M HAPPY.
I'M A HAPPY PERSON.

235
00:09:43,388 --> 00:09:44,689
GO ON AND CRY, BABY.
GO ON AND CRY.

236
00:09:44,689 --> 00:09:45,890
- I'M HAPPY.
- WHY YOU TEARIN' UP?

237
00:09:45,890 --> 00:09:46,891
I'M STRONG.

238
00:09:46,891 --> 00:09:50,028
BECAUSE I WAS THINKING--
I WAS LAYING IN THE BED,

239
00:09:50,028 --> 00:09:52,363
AND I'M, LIKE, I'M LAYING
IN BEVERLY HILLS AGAIN.

240
00:09:52,363 --> 00:09:56,234
AND I SLEEP AT HOME WITH
MY BABY IN A TWIN SIZE BED,

241
00:09:56,234 --> 00:09:58,369
AND I WAS JUST WISHING MY BABY
AND MY GRANDMOTHER--

242
00:09:58,369 --> 00:09:59,537
I REALLY WISH
SHE COULD SEE THIS

243
00:09:59,537 --> 00:10:02,807
'CAUSE SHE AIN'T GOT NO MONEY,
SHE, UM...

244
00:10:02,807 --> 00:10:04,142
THE LAST TIME I WAS HERE,

245
00:10:04,142 --> 00:10:05,910
THEY SAID THAT I NEEDED
TWO BATHING SUITS,

246
00:10:05,910 --> 00:10:08,413
AND SHE WENT AND
SHE BOUGHT ME BATHING SUITS.

247
00:10:08,413 --> 00:10:11,349
THE DAY BEFORE I LEFT,
I WAS, LIKE, GRANDMA, WELL--

248
00:10:11,349 --> 00:10:12,917
YOU KNOW, WHY THE LIGHTS
WENT OFF OR WHATEVER?

249
00:10:12,917 --> 00:10:14,352
SHE WAS, LIKE,
BECAUSE, GIRL,

250
00:10:14,352 --> 00:10:16,554
SOMEBODY AIN'T GETTING PAID
'CAUSE YOU GOIN'.

251
00:10:16,554 --> 00:10:19,557
MY GRANDMOTHER LET THE LIGHTS
GO OFF TO BUY ME A BATHING SUIT.

252
00:10:19,557 --> 00:10:21,392
I LOVE HER SO MUCH.

253
00:10:21,392 --> 00:10:24,028
I JUST WANT TO SHOW MY SON
AND MY FAMILY AS WELL

254
00:10:24,028 --> 00:10:25,930
THAT I CAN DO BETTER.

255
00:10:25,930 --> 00:10:29,434
TIFFANY GRABBED
HER PROBLEMS BY THE REINS.

256
00:10:29,434 --> 00:10:31,536
SHE GOT IT TOGETHER,
SHE CAME BACK,

257
00:10:31,536 --> 00:10:34,138
AND I TRULY BELIEVED

258
00:10:34,138 --> 00:10:37,809
THAT THAT GIRL WANTS
TO CHANGE HER LIFE.

259
00:10:37,809 --> 00:10:39,777
BUT CAN SHE BE A MODEL?

260
00:10:40,878 --> 00:10:44,215
♪♪♪

261
00:10:45,616 --> 00:10:48,886
- OH, IT'S COLD!
- IT IS NOT COLD.

262
00:10:54,359 --> 00:10:55,660
THAT NIGHT
DID THE POOL THING.

263
00:10:55,660 --> 00:10:57,695
I AM GOING TO GET TO KNOW
SOME OF THESE GIRLS.

264
00:10:57,695 --> 00:10:59,897
LIKE, NOW I'M GONNA GET
TO KNOW WHO IS COMPETITIVE.

265
00:11:03,134 --> 00:11:06,437
WE GOT IN THE HOT TUB,
PLAYED SOME TRUTH OR DARE.

266
00:11:06,437 --> 00:11:07,739
SOME PEOPLE GOT
A LITTLE CRAZY.

267
00:11:08,840 --> 00:11:10,375
- ALL RIGHT.
- YOU TWO, RUN DOWN THERE,

268
00:11:10,375 --> 00:11:11,843
SWITCH SWIM SUITS
AND COME BACK.

269
00:11:13,177 --> 00:11:14,912
PEOPLE WERE SO SURPRISED
'CAUSE THEY THOUGHT,

270
00:11:14,912 --> 00:11:16,114
I DON'T KNOW,
JUST BECAUSE I WAS PLUS,

271
00:11:16,114 --> 00:11:18,149
I WOULD BE SHY
ABOUT MY BODY.

272
00:11:18,149 --> 00:11:19,650
BUT I WAS RIPPING OFF
MY CLOTHES.

273
00:11:19,650 --> 00:11:21,419
THIS IS NOT
"GIRLS GONE WILD."

274
00:11:21,419 --> 00:11:24,122
- (applause)
- YOU GO, GIRL!

275
00:11:24,122 --> 00:11:25,923
I AM JUST GONNA BE EXACTLY
WHO I AM.

276
00:11:28,526 --> 00:11:32,663
ME AND A FEW OF THE GIRLS
WERE JUST, LIKE, POLE DANCES!

277
00:11:32,663 --> 00:11:35,566
I'M, LIKE, GUYS, THAT IS NOT
THE WAY TO GO.

278
00:11:35,566 --> 00:11:36,934
OH, LET'S GET NAKED.

279
00:11:36,934 --> 00:11:38,636
OH, MY GOD!

280
00:11:38,636 --> 00:11:40,805
I WASN'T SITTING THERE
TALKING TO PEOPLE AND GOING,

281
00:11:40,805 --> 00:11:43,174
"YEAH, I AM FROM
TALLAHASSEE, WHEW."

282
00:11:44,542 --> 00:11:45,643
I DON'T THINK
IT WAS A BIG DEAL,

283
00:11:45,643 --> 00:11:47,678
BUT I LIKE TO SEE PEOPLE
DO CRAZY STUFF.

284
00:11:49,547 --> 00:11:51,315
I DON'T FEEL I NEED
TO TAKE MY CLOTHES OFF.

285
00:11:51,315 --> 00:11:53,184
I DON'T KNOW IF THAT'S WHO
THESE GIRLS REALLY ARE.

286
00:11:53,184 --> 00:11:55,019
I'M REALLY INTERESTED
TO SEE WHAT'S GONNA HAPPEN

287
00:11:55,019 --> 00:11:56,020
FROM HERE ON OUT.

288
00:12:02,560 --> 00:12:04,395
- WE'RE ALL GOING TO GO OUT.
- WHOO!

289
00:12:04,395 --> 00:12:05,730
I'M JUST TOTALLY PSYCHED.

290
00:12:07,064 --> 00:12:08,399
IF YOU'RE 21 AND OVER,
YOU'RE GOIN'

291
00:12:08,399 --> 00:12:11,169
TO THE TWO HOTTEST CLUBS
IN L.A.

292
00:12:11,169 --> 00:12:14,272
IF YOU'RE UNDER 21,
IT'S A SURPRISE.

293
00:12:17,608 --> 00:12:19,110
OH, YEAH.

294
00:12:19,110 --> 00:12:20,111
I DIDN'T EVEN KNOW
WHERE WE WERE.

295
00:12:20,111 --> 00:12:21,112
I WAS LOOKIN'
AT THE STREET SIGNS.

296
00:12:21,112 --> 00:12:23,114
I SAW SANTA MONICA
AND I SAW SUNSET.

297
00:12:23,114 --> 00:12:24,749
SO THAT WAS REALLY EXCITING.

298
00:12:26,818 --> 00:12:28,052
WE WENT
TO THE WHITE LOTUS.

299
00:12:28,052 --> 00:12:29,320
IT WAS A LOT OF FUN,

300
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:31,389
ESPECIALLY TO GET OUT
AND JUST HAVE FRESH AIR.

301
00:12:35,593 --> 00:12:37,094
WE'RE PRAYING, LIKE,
LET US GO TO THE CLUB,

302
00:12:37,094 --> 00:12:38,663
LET US GO TO THE CLUB.

303
00:12:38,663 --> 00:12:39,764
WHERE THE HELL ARE WE?

304
00:12:41,199 --> 00:12:43,301
HUH.
BOWLING?

305
00:12:43,301 --> 00:12:45,570
WHAT I'M GON' DO IN A...

306
00:12:45,570 --> 00:12:47,071
I WAS LIKE,
I CAN'T EVEN BOWL.

307
00:12:47,071 --> 00:12:49,974
♪♪♪

308
00:12:56,514 --> 00:12:58,349
AND WE ARE GETTING
OUR FREAK ON.

309
00:12:58,349 --> 00:13:00,184
HERE'S TO BEING 21.

310
00:13:01,986 --> 00:13:02,987
NO BOWLING.

311
00:13:02,987 --> 00:13:05,756
♪♪♪

312
00:13:09,560 --> 00:13:11,229
WE ENDED UP
HAVING A BLAST.

313
00:13:18,736 --> 00:13:20,705
IT TURNS OUT WE GOT TO STAY
LATER AT THE BOWLING ALLEY

314
00:13:20,705 --> 00:13:21,939
THAN THEY GOT TO STAY
AT THE CLUB.

315
00:13:21,939 --> 00:13:23,508
NEENER, NEENER, NEENER.

316
00:13:27,612 --> 00:13:28,779
JUST ALL OVER THE PLACE.

317
00:13:28,779 --> 00:13:31,215
OH, MY GOD, OH, MY GOD.
OH, MY GOD.

318
00:13:31,215 --> 00:13:33,885
YOU WALKIN' IN HERE
LIKE YOU'RE NUTS.

319
00:13:33,885 --> 00:13:35,286
MY NAME IS JESSICA.

320
00:13:35,286 --> 00:13:37,889
I'M FROM HOUSTON, TEXAS,
AND I'M 21,

321
00:13:37,889 --> 00:13:40,791
AND I'M KNOWN
AS LADY KAT. RAWR.

322
00:13:40,791 --> 00:13:42,760
WHY DO YOU CALL YOURSELF
LADY KAT?

323
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:45,363
I HAVE LONG NAILS
AND I'LL SCRATCH.

324
00:13:45,363 --> 00:13:47,532
YOUR FACE LOOKS KIND OF
CAT-LIKE TO ME, THE EYES.

325
00:13:47,532 --> 00:13:48,699
YOU WANT TO SEE
THE CAT WALK?

326
00:13:48,699 --> 00:13:50,001
- OH.
- HOLD UP.

327
00:13:50,001 --> 00:13:52,403
- YEAH, WORK IT OUT.
- RAWR. MMM.

328
00:13:55,840 --> 00:13:57,141
SALT TASTES GOOD.

329
00:13:57,141 --> 00:13:58,643
I HOPE I'M GETTIN'
LOTS OF CHOCOLATE.

330
00:14:01,012 --> 00:14:04,148
I'M AGGRESSIVE AND I AM,
I WON'T SAY ARROGANT,

331
00:14:04,148 --> 00:14:05,750
BUT JUST THIS
PASSIONATE INDIVIDUAL.

332
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:07,652
- HOW TALL ARE YOU?
- I ACTUALLY--I DON'T KNOW.

333
00:14:07,652 --> 00:14:09,453
- STAND UP, TYRA.
- TAKE YOUR SHOES OFF.

334
00:14:09,453 --> 00:14:11,188
I CAN TELL YOU
HOW TALL YOU ARE.

335
00:14:11,188 --> 00:14:13,491
- I'M 5'10".
- I THINK YOU'RE 5'9".

336
00:14:13,491 --> 00:14:15,092
OH, MY GOD, I WAS STANDING--
CAN I TOUCH YOU?

337
00:14:15,092 --> 00:14:16,160
OOH!

338
00:14:16,160 --> 00:14:17,828
MY GOD. OH!

339
00:14:17,828 --> 00:14:19,397
- BYE.
- RAWR.

340
00:14:19,397 --> 00:14:21,032
- RAWR.
- RAWR.

341
00:14:21,032 --> 00:14:22,066
DO YOU KNOW
WHAT'S SO FUNNY?

342
00:14:22,066 --> 00:14:23,734
I DIDN'T REALIZE HOW
BEAUTIFUL HER SKIN IS

343
00:14:23,734 --> 00:14:25,202
- WHEN SHE WALKED IN.
- SHE IS GORGEOUS.

344
00:14:25,202 --> 00:14:26,604
I LIKED HER.

345
00:14:26,604 --> 00:14:28,172
HI, I'M SARAH.

346
00:14:28,172 --> 00:14:29,607
GROWING UP,
I WAS THE TOMBOY.

347
00:14:29,607 --> 00:14:32,610
MY OLDER SISTER USED TO TELL ME
THAT I WASN'T REALLY PRETTY

348
00:14:32,610 --> 00:14:33,644
OR ANYTHING LIKE THAT.

349
00:14:33,644 --> 00:14:34,679
YOU'RE NOT GOOD ENOUGH,
YOU'RE NOT PRETTY ENOUGH,

350
00:14:34,679 --> 00:14:35,680
YOU'RE NOT TALL ENOUGH.

351
00:14:35,680 --> 00:14:36,981
YOU KNOW, LIKE,
THAT SUCKS,

352
00:14:36,981 --> 00:14:38,082
BUT YOU JUST MOVE ON.

353
00:14:38,082 --> 00:14:40,985
VERY SKINNY AND STRAIGHT
AND NO BOOB, NO NOTHING,

354
00:14:40,985 --> 00:14:43,588
NOT UNTIL I WAS, LIKE
16 YEARS OLD, 17 YEARS OLD

355
00:14:43,588 --> 00:14:46,190
THAT I FINALLY GREW, LIKE,
A CHEST AT ALL.

356
00:14:46,190 --> 00:14:47,191
I JUST KIND OF BLOSSOMED.

357
00:14:47,191 --> 00:14:48,492
I GUESS IT JUST TOOK ME
A LITTLE WHILE.

358
00:14:48,492 --> 00:14:50,261
- WHAT DOES THAT SAY?
- "HOLLA BACK," GIRL.

359
00:14:50,261 --> 00:14:51,762
- HOLLA BACK.
- WHOO! WHOO!

360
00:14:51,762 --> 00:14:52,830
SHE HAD A NICE WAIST.

361
00:14:52,830 --> 00:14:53,831
I THOUGHT
SHE HAD GREAT SKIN.

362
00:14:53,831 --> 00:14:56,267
REALLY BIG PERSONALITY,
FUN, FUN, FUN.

363
00:14:56,267 --> 00:14:57,535
I JUST DIDN'T
HOLLA BACK.

364
00:14:59,403 --> 00:15:01,939
HI, EVERYBODY,
I'M LLUVY.

365
00:15:01,939 --> 00:15:03,441
SORRY.
I'M REALLY NERVOUS.

366
00:15:03,441 --> 00:15:05,276
- LLUVY, IS THAT YOUR DRESS?
- MM-MMM.

367
00:15:05,276 --> 00:15:07,912
- ACTUALLY, IT IS MY SISTER'S.
- I KNEW IT.

368
00:15:07,912 --> 00:15:09,680
- I KNEW IT WASN'T YOURS.
- NO?

369
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:11,248
- YEAH. I COULD TELL.
- I AM A JEANS AND
A T-SHIRT GIRL.

370
00:15:11,248 --> 00:15:13,484
I KNOW. DO YOU HAVE
JEANS AND T-SHIRT HERE?

371
00:15:13,484 --> 00:15:15,620
CAN YOU GO BACK
AND PUT THOSE ON?

372
00:15:15,620 --> 00:15:16,954
- YEAH.
- 'CAUSE I CAN TELL
THAT'S NOT YOU.

373
00:15:16,954 --> 00:15:18,222
OH, THANK YOU.
I LOVE YOU.

374
00:15:20,725 --> 00:15:22,360
THERE SHE IS.

375
00:15:22,360 --> 00:15:23,661
YOU'RE YOURSELF RIGHT NOW.

376
00:15:23,661 --> 00:15:25,997
YEAH. THANK YOU GUYS
SO MUCH. I APPRECIATE THAT.

377
00:15:25,997 --> 00:15:29,467
WHEN I WAS A KID, I WENT
THROUGH BASICALLY EVERY STAGE

378
00:15:29,467 --> 00:15:31,235
THAT YOU CAN THINK OF.

379
00:15:31,235 --> 00:15:32,937
LLUVY, ON YOUR
APPLICATION IT SAYS

380
00:15:32,937 --> 00:15:33,904
YOU USED TO BE IN A GANG.

381
00:15:35,172 --> 00:15:36,574
OH, GOODNESS ME.

382
00:15:36,574 --> 00:15:38,309
BEING IN A GANG AND
DOING ALL THAT STUFF--

383
00:15:38,309 --> 00:15:40,611
I THINK IT'S THE WORST,
LIKE, STAGE OF MY LIFE.

384
00:15:40,611 --> 00:15:43,047
I WAS JUST AN ANGRY KID.
IT'S SAD.

385
00:15:43,047 --> 00:15:44,215
LIKE, I HATE
TALKING ABOUT IT

386
00:15:44,215 --> 00:15:46,584
BECAUSE IT GETS ME
KINDA ALL LOOPY.

387
00:15:46,584 --> 00:15:49,020
BUT I JUST HAD A LOT OF,
LIKE, RESENTMENT

388
00:15:49,020 --> 00:15:50,321
AGAINST A LOT OF PEOPLE,

389
00:15:50,321 --> 00:15:52,323
ESPECIALLY NOT HAVING
A DAD AND STUFF.

390
00:15:52,323 --> 00:15:54,392
MY DAD PASSED AWAY
WHEN I WAS 3.

391
00:15:54,392 --> 00:15:57,328
THE ONE THING THAT
I CLEARLY REMEMBER GROWING UP

392
00:15:57,328 --> 00:15:58,729
IS MY MOM ALWAYS
TELLING ME,

393
00:15:58,729 --> 00:16:00,898
"YOUR DAD ALWAYS
WANTED YOU TO BE A MODEL."

394
00:16:00,898 --> 00:16:03,300
SO I JUST KNOW--I'M LIKE,
OKAY, I HAVE TO BE A MODEL.

395
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:05,002
I THINK SHE'S GREAT.

396
00:16:05,002 --> 00:16:07,271
I LOVE HER.

397
00:16:09,006 --> 00:16:10,141
HI, MY NAME IS MICHELLE.

398
00:16:10,141 --> 00:16:12,376
I AM 18
AND I'M FROM INDIANA.

399
00:16:12,376 --> 00:16:15,413
I AM PART OF THIS WRESTLING
FEDERATION IN INDIANA.

400
00:16:15,413 --> 00:16:16,981
THIS IS WHAT HAPPENS.

401
00:16:19,784 --> 00:16:22,653
AND USUALLY WHEN I GET UP
ON THE SIDE OF THE RING,

402
00:16:22,653 --> 00:16:24,655
I DO A BACK FLIP
INTO IT OFF THE ROPE.

403
00:16:24,655 --> 00:16:27,058
LIKE, THE GIRLS I WRESTLE
ARE, LIKE, 125 POUNDS,

404
00:16:27,058 --> 00:16:29,260
AND I, LIKE, HAVE TO
BE ABLE TO PICK THEM UP

405
00:16:29,260 --> 00:16:31,062
AND KIND OF, LIKE,
FLING 'EM AROUND.

406
00:16:31,062 --> 00:16:32,396
I'LL GO OUT THERE
AND I'LL JUST, LIKE,

407
00:16:32,396 --> 00:16:33,397
DO MY LITTLE POSE

408
00:16:33,397 --> 00:16:35,533
AND EVERYONE'S, LIKE,
"BOO, BOO."

409
00:16:35,533 --> 00:16:37,835
I LOVE WRESTLING A LOT.

410
00:16:37,835 --> 00:16:42,506
BUT I WILL SACRIFICE THE
WRESTLING TO BECOME A MODEL.

411
00:16:42,506 --> 00:16:44,308
I WANT TO BE THE NEXT
TYRA BANKS, DAMN IT.

412
00:16:46,143 --> 00:16:48,179
LOST MY SHOE.
HOLD ON A SECOND.

413
00:16:48,179 --> 00:16:50,915
♪ YEAH ♪

414
00:16:50,915 --> 00:16:56,020
♪ AMERICA'S TOP MODEL
IS IN HERE, YEAH ♪

415
00:16:56,020 --> 00:16:58,789
- WALK OUT.
- OH, NO! OH, NO, YOU DIDN'T.

416
00:16:58,789 --> 00:17:00,458
TO BE, LIKE, AN
INSPIRATIONAL SPEACHER--

417
00:17:00,458 --> 00:17:01,792
- SPEAK--
- MNH-MNH.

418
00:17:01,792 --> 00:17:03,461
I AM NOT
A VIRGIN ANYMORE.

419
00:17:03,461 --> 00:17:04,962
YOU AREN'T EITHER.

420
00:17:04,962 --> 00:17:05,996
I DO THE BEYONCE.

421
00:17:08,365 --> 00:17:10,668
OH, HERE GOES THE BEAT.
OOH, WAIT. UH, UH...

422
00:17:14,637 --> 00:17:17,308
(classical music playing)

423
00:17:22,378 --> 00:17:23,614
LOVE THE BLOOMERS.

424
00:17:25,049 --> 00:17:26,517
HOW DO YOU PRONOUNCE
YOUR NAME?

425
00:17:26,517 --> 00:17:27,518
NAIMA.

426
00:17:27,518 --> 00:17:28,853
MY PARENTS
ARE MUSICIANS.

427
00:17:28,853 --> 00:17:30,988
AND JOHN COLTRANE
IS A JAZZ MUSICIAN.

428
00:17:30,988 --> 00:17:34,157
THEY NAMED ME AFTER
A COMPOSITION OF HIS

429
00:17:34,157 --> 00:17:35,392
NAMED "NAIMA."

430
00:17:35,392 --> 00:17:37,061
TELL ME ABOUT THIS MOHAWK.

431
00:17:37,061 --> 00:17:40,397
I HAD LONG HAIR, AND
THERE WAS JUST SO MANY THINGS

432
00:17:40,397 --> 00:17:43,033
I WAS CARRYING AROUND WITH ME
FROM MY PAST

433
00:17:43,033 --> 00:17:46,203
AND MY CHILDHOOD AND
JUST CRAZINESS IN MY HEAD,

434
00:17:46,203 --> 00:17:47,338
AND I JUST WANTED
TO GET RID OF IT.

435
00:17:47,338 --> 00:17:48,839
I JUST KINDA WANTED
TO BECOME A MONK,

436
00:17:48,839 --> 00:17:49,907
SO I JUST SHAVED MY HEAD.

437
00:17:49,907 --> 00:17:52,877
AND I DECIDED A MOHAWK
WOULD BE IDEAL

438
00:17:52,877 --> 00:17:55,045
SO IT COULD
CENSOR MY THOUGHTS.

439
00:17:55,045 --> 00:17:56,714
HEY.

440
00:17:56,714 --> 00:17:57,982
MY FELLOW REDHEAD SISTER.

441
00:17:57,982 --> 00:18:00,384
POWER TO THE PEOPLE.

442
00:18:00,384 --> 00:18:02,419
I'M BRANDY.

443
00:18:02,419 --> 00:18:04,789
I'M 19, AND I AM
FROM HOUSTON, TEXAS.

444
00:18:04,789 --> 00:18:06,090
CAN I JUST SAY SOMETHING?

445
00:18:06,090 --> 00:18:07,424
I AM SO JEALOUS
OF YOUR HAIR

446
00:18:07,424 --> 00:18:10,060
'CAUSE IT WAS JUST, LIKE,
BOUNCING LEFT AND RIGHT.

447
00:18:10,060 --> 00:18:11,729
- IT'S BEAUTIFUL.
- THANK YOU.

448
00:18:11,729 --> 00:18:13,464
YOURS IS BEAUTIFUL, TOO.
IT'S JUST NATURAL.

449
00:18:13,464 --> 00:18:14,865
I BET YOUR HAIR,
STRAIGHTENED,

450
00:18:14,865 --> 00:18:16,200
IT'D BE, LIKE,
WAY DOWN TO HERE.

451
00:18:16,200 --> 00:18:17,668
NO, GIRL, IT'S NOT REAL.

452
00:18:17,668 --> 00:18:19,336
IT IS NOT REAL?

453
00:18:19,336 --> 00:18:21,572
- IT'S NOT REAL.
- WHAT IS IT?

454
00:18:21,572 --> 00:18:23,073
IT'S SEWN IN.

455
00:18:23,073 --> 00:18:24,275
MY MOTHER DID IT.

456
00:18:24,275 --> 00:18:25,876
TELL YOUR MAMA
I AIN'T MAD AT HER.

457
00:18:25,876 --> 00:18:27,011
THIS IS BRANDY.

458
00:18:27,011 --> 00:18:28,612
IF YOU DON'T LIKE IT,
YOU AIN'T GOT TO LIKE IT,

459
00:18:28,612 --> 00:18:30,581
BUT I LOVE IT AND LIKE IT
SO THAT'S ME.

460
00:18:30,581 --> 00:18:33,317
COMPETITION--
THAT'S THE BIGGEST WORD

461
00:18:33,317 --> 00:18:34,451
IN MY HEAD RIGHT NOW,

462
00:18:34,451 --> 00:18:36,520
AND I AM GOING TO BE
ABOUT WINNING.

463
00:18:36,520 --> 00:18:37,922
YOU NEED A SHIRT?

464
00:18:37,922 --> 00:18:39,323
YOU SHOULDA BROUGHT
YOUR OWN.

465
00:18:39,323 --> 00:18:41,892
MM-HMM.

466
00:18:41,892 --> 00:18:43,260
- THANK YOU. BYE.
- BYE.

467
00:18:43,260 --> 00:18:46,130
WALK? IT'S LIKE
SHE DIDN'T TRY AT ALL.

468
00:18:46,130 --> 00:18:49,500
IT WAS LIKE SHE WAS WALKING
DOWN THE GROCERY LINE,

469
00:18:49,500 --> 00:18:51,068
AND I'M GONNA GET
SOME CANNED PEACHES.

470
00:18:51,068 --> 00:18:52,736
- LIKE, I DIDN'T FEEL LIKE--
- SOME CANNED PEACHES?

471
00:18:52,736 --> 00:18:54,805
SERIOUSLY.

472
00:18:54,805 --> 00:18:56,073
- HI.
- HI.

473
00:18:56,073 --> 00:18:58,442
MY NAME'S TATIANA
I'M FROM MAUI, HAWAII,

474
00:18:58,442 --> 00:19:00,744
AND I'M 18.
ALOHA.

475
00:19:00,744 --> 00:19:01,712
MAHALO.

476
00:19:01,712 --> 00:19:04,849
I WAS DRIVING,
AND I HEARD IT ON THE RADIO.

477
00:19:04,849 --> 00:19:07,618
THERE'S "TOP MODEL"
AUDITIONS IN OAHU.

478
00:19:07,618 --> 00:19:09,320
AND I, LIKE,
WENT TO THE AIRPORT,

479
00:19:09,320 --> 00:19:12,690
SPENT ALL MY RENT MONEY
ON A PLANE TICKET.

480
00:19:12,690 --> 00:19:15,125
IF I WANT SOMETHING,
I WILL MAKE IT HAPPEN.

481
00:19:15,125 --> 00:19:16,527
YOU SAID THAT YOU LEFT
HIGH SCHOOL.

482
00:19:16,527 --> 00:19:18,329
I LIKE TO LEARN
BY MYSELF, BY, LIKE,

483
00:19:18,329 --> 00:19:19,730
MAKING MY OWN MISTAKES.

484
00:19:19,730 --> 00:19:20,731
I'M GONNA GO GET
MY G.E.D.

485
00:19:20,731 --> 00:19:22,266
AND I'M GONNA PURSUE
WHAT I WANT TO DO,

486
00:19:22,266 --> 00:19:23,834
- WHICH IS MODELING.
- THANK YOU.

487
00:19:23,834 --> 00:19:25,936
- THANKS.
- THANK YOU, GUYS.

488
00:19:25,936 --> 00:19:28,105
- I LIKE HER.
- AND SHE'S GOT PERSONALITY.

489
00:19:29,473 --> 00:19:31,342
HI, MY NAME IS ESTELA.

490
00:19:31,342 --> 00:19:34,879
I'M 22 YEARS OLD,
AND I AM FROM THE BRONX.

491
00:19:34,879 --> 00:19:37,815
THIS WHOLE COMPETITION
IS INSIDE ME RIGHT NOW.

492
00:19:37,815 --> 00:19:40,217
I JUST WANT IT SO BAD,
I TASTE IT.

493
00:19:40,217 --> 00:19:41,852
THIS IS WHAT'S
GONNA GIVE ME

494
00:19:41,852 --> 00:19:45,089
A BETTER LIFE FOR ME
AND MY BABY GIRL.

495
00:19:45,089 --> 00:19:46,156
HOW OLD IS YOUR DAUGHTER?

496
00:19:46,156 --> 00:19:47,858
SHE'S GONNA BE
3 YEARS OLD.

497
00:19:47,858 --> 00:19:50,728
I GOT MARRIED AT 18,
AND WE WERE VERY MUCH IN LOVE,

498
00:19:50,728 --> 00:19:53,864
PLANNED PREGNANCY AND ALL,
AND THEN, UM,

499
00:19:53,864 --> 00:19:56,066
HE DIDN'T WANT US NO MORE.

500
00:19:56,066 --> 00:19:59,136
IT'S HARD FOR ME BECAUSE
I DID EVERYTHING BY THE BOOK.

501
00:19:59,136 --> 00:20:01,839
OUR BABY WAS WANTED,
AND THEN MY HUSBAND

502
00:20:01,839 --> 00:20:08,245
PUT ME AND MY DAUGHTER OUT
IN FEBRUARY IN COLD WEATHER.

503
00:20:08,245 --> 00:20:11,782
MY DAUGHTER AND I WERE HOMELESS
AND LIVING IN THE SHELTER.

504
00:20:11,782 --> 00:20:13,317
YOU ARE IN A ROOM
WITH NO SHEETS,

505
00:20:13,317 --> 00:20:17,321
WHERE THE FIRST WARNING YOU GET
IS WATCH OUT WITH THE BED BUGS.

506
00:20:17,321 --> 00:20:19,456
AND YOU HAVE NO SHEETS,
SO YOU HAVE TO STAY

507
00:20:19,456 --> 00:20:21,992
SLEEPING ON A CHAIR,
HOLDING YOUR CHILD.

508
00:20:21,992 --> 00:20:23,494
AND THEN MY DAUGHTER
CRIED FOR MILK,

509
00:20:23,494 --> 00:20:25,429
AND I DIDN'T
HAVE ANY MONEY.

510
00:20:25,429 --> 00:20:27,331
WHEN YOU CAN'T FEED
YOUR OWN KID,

511
00:20:27,331 --> 00:20:29,466
AND THEY'RE LOOKING UP
AT YOU AND CRYING

512
00:20:29,466 --> 00:20:31,168
BECAUSE THEY'RE HUNGRY,
AND YOU'RE, LIKE,

513
00:20:31,168 --> 00:20:32,336
"I DON'T HAVE
THE MONEY." YOU KNOW?

514
00:20:32,336 --> 00:20:33,637
LIKE, "WAIT,
YOU GOTTA WAIT."

515
00:20:33,637 --> 00:20:35,239
I THINK THAT WAS
THE HARDEST.

516
00:20:35,239 --> 00:20:37,408
BUT IT MADE YOU
A STRONG PERSON.

517
00:20:37,408 --> 00:20:41,011
YOU KNOW WHAT? STRONGER
AND STRONGER EVERY DAY.

518
00:20:41,011 --> 00:20:42,279
THANK YOU, ESTELA.

519
00:20:45,382 --> 00:20:46,450
MAYBE SHE IS A DIAMOND
IN THE ROUGH.

520
00:20:48,152 --> 00:20:50,421
THIS COMPETITION
IS A FIGHT TO ME.

521
00:20:50,421 --> 00:20:52,256
I HAVE MY DAUGHTER
TO WIN THIS FOR,

522
00:20:52,256 --> 00:20:53,257
AND MY DAUGHTER'S LIFE.

523
00:20:53,257 --> 00:20:55,993
ALL IT TAKES IS TO
GET MY FOOT IN THAT DOOR,

524
00:20:55,993 --> 00:20:57,761
AND I AM NOT GONNA GET OUT.

525
00:21:01,565 --> 00:21:05,536
♪♪♪

526
00:21:05,536 --> 00:21:07,938
IT WAS THE BIRTHDAY PARTY,
YOU KNOW, FOR TWO GIRLS.

527
00:21:07,938 --> 00:21:09,840
HOLD UP. I AM TALKING.

528
00:21:09,840 --> 00:21:12,242
DING, DING, DING, LADY KAT'S
GOT SOMETHING TO SAY.

529
00:21:12,242 --> 00:21:15,846
EXCUSE ME.
HOLD UP! HOLD UP!

530
00:21:15,846 --> 00:21:17,448
QUIET DOWN, QUIET DOWN,
QUIET DOWN!

531
00:21:17,448 --> 00:21:19,350
REDHEAD OVER THERE,
I DON'T KNOW YOUR NAME.

532
00:21:19,350 --> 00:21:21,819
I THOUGHT THAT WAS-- HOLD UP,
I THOUGHT THAT WAS RUDE.

533
00:21:21,819 --> 00:21:22,953
I GOT SOMETHING TO SAY.

534
00:21:22,953 --> 00:21:24,822
SAY WHATEVER
YOU WANT TO SAY.

535
00:21:24,822 --> 00:21:27,257
Y'ALL NEED TO ALL FIND
A HAPPY PLACE.

536
00:21:27,257 --> 00:21:29,493
LADY KAT--SHE IS A HANDFUL.

537
00:21:29,493 --> 00:21:31,161
CRAZY FREAK.
I SWEAR TO GOD.

538
00:21:31,161 --> 00:21:32,529
SHE NEEDS TO STAY
THE... AWAY FROM ME,

539
00:21:32,529 --> 00:21:33,697
'CAUSE I WILL SLAP HER.

540
00:21:33,697 --> 00:21:35,432
DON'T TELL ME WHAT'S NOT
RIGHT OR WRONG

541
00:21:35,432 --> 00:21:36,734
ABOUT MY PERSONALITY.

542
00:21:36,734 --> 00:21:38,535
SHUT THE... UP!

543
00:21:38,535 --> 00:21:40,237
YOU KNOW, I'M JUST LOOKING
AT THEM, AND I'M, LIKE, "DAMN.

544
00:21:40,237 --> 00:21:41,205
THAT'S THE WAY
I USED TO ACT?"

545
00:21:43,674 --> 00:21:46,010
♪♪♪

546
00:21:46,010 --> 00:21:47,211
I'M, LIKE, READY TO GO OUT,

547
00:21:47,211 --> 00:21:50,280
READY TO GET, LIKE, STRESS
OFF OF MY--OFF OF MY BACK.

548
00:21:52,716 --> 00:21:55,085
WE GET TO GRIFFITH PARK,
WE'RE, LIKE, ALL EXCITED.

549
00:21:55,085 --> 00:21:57,988
WE'RE, LIKE, YAY!
BEING LITTLE GIRLS ABOUT IT.

550
00:21:57,988 --> 00:21:59,289
I LOVE THAT WE ARE
OUTSIDE RIGHT NOW.

551
00:21:59,289 --> 00:22:00,691
IT'S GREAT.

552
00:22:02,092 --> 00:22:03,827
THERE ARE BEES ALL OVER.

553
00:22:06,697 --> 00:22:08,265
(screaming)
THEY ARE EVERYWHERE!

554
00:22:08,265 --> 00:22:10,100
I WAS WALKING THROUGH
THE GRASS, AND THERE'S,

555
00:22:10,100 --> 00:22:11,602
LIKE, BEES JUST FLYING UP
FROM EVERYWHERE

556
00:22:11,602 --> 00:22:14,038
AND I'M NOT USED TO BEES
JUST FLYING AND TOUCHING ME.

557
00:22:14,038 --> 00:22:16,106
YOU NEED TO MOVE, GIRL.
YOU NEED TO MOVE.

558
00:22:16,106 --> 00:22:17,007
WE'LL WALK THIS WAY.

559
00:22:22,880 --> 00:22:24,114
DURING THE BIRTHDAY
CELEBRATION,

560
00:22:24,114 --> 00:22:25,482
LADY KAT
CUSSED EVERYBODY OUT.

561
00:22:25,482 --> 00:22:27,518
HOLD UP, HOLD UP, HOLD UP.

562
00:22:27,518 --> 00:22:29,219
SHE'S A LITTLE LIKE ME.

563
00:22:29,219 --> 00:22:30,988
I USED TO BE LIKE HER.

564
00:22:30,988 --> 00:22:32,723
BE ON YOUR BEST BEHAVIOR,
'CAUSE IT'S NOT WORTH IT.

565
00:22:32,723 --> 00:22:35,125
YOU'RE HERE FOR A REASON,
NOT TO BEAT UP ON EVERYBODY.

566
00:22:35,125 --> 00:22:37,294
I FELT THAT WAS MY PLACE,
TO STEP IN AND GIVE HER

567
00:22:37,294 --> 00:22:39,830
THE MOST ADVICE THAT I CAN,
YOU KNOW, JUST CHILL.

568
00:22:39,830 --> 00:22:42,066
BUT I'M STILL
COMPETING AGAINST HER.

569
00:22:42,066 --> 00:22:44,435
THESE BEES ARE CRAZY.

570
00:22:44,435 --> 00:22:45,736
OH, TAKE THAT.

571
00:22:46,870 --> 00:22:48,772
(laughter)

572
00:22:53,844 --> 00:22:55,212
HELLO.

573
00:22:55,212 --> 00:22:58,182
MY NAME IS MARY,
AND THIS IS MY SECOND CHANCE.

574
00:22:58,182 --> 00:23:00,617
GOOD SEEIN' YOU AGAIN.

575
00:23:01,785 --> 00:23:02,886
I AM NOT GONNA PULL BACK,

576
00:23:02,886 --> 00:23:05,022
I'M NOT GONNA NOT SHOW MY
EMOTION WHEN I SHOULD'VE,

577
00:23:05,022 --> 00:23:06,690
SO THEY REALLY KNOW
WHO I AM.

578
00:23:06,690 --> 00:23:07,691
WHAT WAS GOIN'
THROUGH YOUR MIND

579
00:23:07,691 --> 00:23:08,826
WHEN YOU DIDN'T MAKE IT
LAST TIME?

580
00:23:08,826 --> 00:23:11,161
I FELT LIKE SOMETHING
HAD JUST BEEN RIPPED OUT.

581
00:23:11,161 --> 00:23:12,229
THIS IS THE FIRST TIME
IN MY LIFE

582
00:23:12,229 --> 00:23:14,565
I FELT LIKE I'D BEEN ALIVE,
LIKE, I WAS, LIKE, WOW,

583
00:23:14,565 --> 00:23:16,233
I'M DOIN' WHAT I WANT
TO DO, AND I'M SO EXCITED,

584
00:23:16,233 --> 00:23:17,501
AND I'M SO CONFIDENT.

585
00:23:17,501 --> 00:23:20,137
AND THEN, I DON'T KNOW,
IT WAS HORRIBLE.

586
00:23:20,137 --> 00:23:21,105
I HOPE THIS CAN
HAPPEN FOR ME.

587
00:23:22,172 --> 00:23:23,707
SO, RACHEL,
WHY ARE YOU HERE?

588
00:23:23,707 --> 00:23:25,809
WHY AM I HERE? WHY NOT?

589
00:23:25,809 --> 00:23:27,978
YOU'D BE REPRESENTING
MORE OF A PLUS SIZE.

590
00:23:27,978 --> 00:23:29,213
I'M DOWN WITH THAT.

591
00:23:29,213 --> 00:23:34,651
MY COMPETITION IS EVERYBODY,
WHETHER THEY ARE SKINNY AND TALL

592
00:23:34,651 --> 00:23:36,887
OR VOLUPTUOUS AND
LARGER THAN ME.

593
00:23:38,288 --> 00:23:40,891
ANYTHING THAT I CAN DO,
I'LL DO IT.

594
00:23:40,891 --> 00:23:42,826
AS LONG AS
I AIN'T SHOWING NIPPLE,

595
00:23:42,826 --> 00:23:44,094
I'M GOOD TO GO.

596
00:23:44,094 --> 00:23:45,329
MY GRANDPARENTS ARE DEAD.

597
00:23:45,329 --> 00:23:46,964
I HAVE NO ONE
TO DISGRACE.

598
00:23:46,964 --> 00:23:48,031
HI.

599
00:23:48,031 --> 00:23:49,800
MY NAME IS ALEXANDRIA.

600
00:23:49,800 --> 00:23:54,238
I AM 19, AND I AM FROM
FORT COLLINS, COLORADO.

601
00:23:54,238 --> 00:23:56,773
GROWING UP, THEY KINDA
WANTED ME IN SPECIAL ED,

602
00:23:56,773 --> 00:23:59,843
JUST BECAUSE I HAD A REALLY
BAD SPEECH IMPEDIMENT.

603
00:23:59,843 --> 00:24:01,311
THEY ACTUALLY HAD ME
ON THE SHORT BUS.

604
00:24:01,311 --> 00:24:03,247
"OH, THE SPECIAL BUS
IS WAITING FOR YOU."

605
00:24:03,247 --> 00:24:06,383
A LOT OF ACTORS AND MODELS
AND A LOT OF MUSICIANS

606
00:24:06,383 --> 00:24:08,085
RODE THE SHORT BUS
TO SCHOOL.

607
00:24:08,085 --> 00:24:10,754
I DON'T KNOW IF YOU KNOW
THAT, BUT IT'S TRUE.

608
00:24:10,754 --> 00:24:11,822
NO BIG DEAL.

609
00:24:11,822 --> 00:24:13,023
I SEE MYSELF

610
00:24:13,023 --> 00:24:15,025
DOING SOMETHING EXTRAORDINARY
WITH MY LIFE.

611
00:24:15,025 --> 00:24:16,860
HAVING PEOPLE
SEE ME FOR WHO I AM.

612
00:24:16,860 --> 00:24:18,562
- BYE.
- BYE.

613
00:24:19,830 --> 00:24:20,998
MY NAME'S CHRISTINA.

614
00:24:20,998 --> 00:24:23,033
I'M 24,
AND I LIVE IN TALLAHASSEE

615
00:24:23,033 --> 00:24:24,067
AND GO TO FLORIDA STATE.

616
00:24:24,067 --> 00:24:25,269
DO YOU TAN?

617
00:24:25,269 --> 00:24:26,770
I DO LAY OUT,
SOMETIMES, YES.

618
00:24:26,770 --> 00:24:28,739
OKAY, YOU LOOKIN' LIKE
MY COUSIN.

619
00:24:28,739 --> 00:24:30,908
YOU LOOKIN' A LITTLE
NEGRO OVER THERE.

620
00:24:30,908 --> 00:24:32,109
I'M FROM FLORIDA. SORRY.

621
00:24:32,109 --> 00:24:34,378
YOU SEEM TO HAVE A, LIKE,
A REALLY TOUGH EXTERIOR.

622
00:24:34,378 --> 00:24:35,412
I MEAN,
I DO HAVE CONFIDENCE.

623
00:24:35,412 --> 00:24:37,281
AND I'M NOT GONNA LIE,
I AM NOT COCKY, BUT I DO,

624
00:24:37,281 --> 00:24:39,116
LIKE, CARRY MYSELF WELL.
I ALWAYS HAVE.

625
00:24:39,116 --> 00:24:40,284
WHEN PEOPLE FIRST MEET ME,
THEY'RE LIKE,

626
00:24:40,284 --> 00:24:42,152
"OH, SHE'S STUCK UP."
YOU KNOW WHAT?

627
00:24:42,152 --> 00:24:44,188
IT REALLY DOESN'T EVEN
FAZE ME ANYMORE.

628
00:24:45,956 --> 00:24:47,958
- (Foreign accent) BRITA.
- (Foreign accent) HI, BRITA.

629
00:24:47,958 --> 00:24:48,992
HI. HOW ARE YOU GUYS?

630
00:24:48,992 --> 00:24:50,794
DID YOUR MOM AND DADDY
TALK LIKE THIS?

631
00:24:50,794 --> 00:24:51,929
YES.

632
00:24:51,929 --> 00:24:53,931
MY PARENTS
ARE FROM LATVIA.

633
00:24:53,931 --> 00:24:56,400
- (normal voice) WHERE IS THAT?
- IT'S NEXT TO LITHUANIA,

634
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:58,035
WHICH MORE PEOPLE
HAVE HEARD OF.

635
00:24:58,035 --> 00:25:01,638
GROWING UP, I MIGHT HAVE
BEEN TRAVELING THE WORLD.

636
00:25:01,638 --> 00:25:03,507
THIS IS MY FRONT DOOR.

637
00:25:03,507 --> 00:25:06,376
WE HAD A NICE HOUSE,
WE HAD DECENT CARS.

638
00:25:06,376 --> 00:25:07,844
SO YOU GREW UP
REALLY WEALTHY?

639
00:25:07,844 --> 00:25:09,746
PRETTY WEALTHY,
COMPARED TO MOST PEOPLE.

640
00:25:09,746 --> 00:25:11,114
AND NOW YOU'RE
A WAITRESS.

641
00:25:11,114 --> 00:25:12,983
MY DAD BROKE HIS BACK,

642
00:25:12,983 --> 00:25:15,152
SO HE COULDN'T
SUPPORT OUR FAMILY.

643
00:25:15,152 --> 00:25:16,920
PRETTY MUCH, I'VE JUST
BEEN KIND OF ON MY OWN.

644
00:25:16,920 --> 00:25:17,921
I PAY MY OWN BILLS.

645
00:25:17,921 --> 00:25:19,990
PEOPLE TALK DOWN TO ME
BECAUSE I AM A WAITRESS.

646
00:25:19,990 --> 00:25:21,091
THAT'S FINE.

647
00:25:21,091 --> 00:25:22,526
I AM TRYING TO STRIVE
FOR SOMETHING ELSE.

648
00:25:23,627 --> 00:25:24,661
THAT'S WHY I AM HERE.

649
00:25:24,661 --> 00:25:25,896
I'M TRYING
TO PURSUE MY DREAM.

650
00:25:27,698 --> 00:25:28,765
MY NAME'S NOELLE

651
00:25:28,765 --> 00:25:30,901
AND I'M REPRESENTIN'
RENO, NEVADA.

652
00:25:30,901 --> 00:25:33,570
THIS IS A PICTURE
OF ME AND MY SON.

653
00:25:33,570 --> 00:25:34,972
I HAD A BABY
KIND OF YOUNG.

654
00:25:34,972 --> 00:25:36,340
NOT THAT I REGRET IT
AT ALL.

655
00:25:36,340 --> 00:25:38,108
TELL ME YOUR EXPERIENCE
ABOUT BEING YOUNG

656
00:25:38,108 --> 00:25:40,711
AND BEING PREGNANT,
THE GUY.

657
00:25:40,711 --> 00:25:41,912
WELL, I'M STILL WITH HIM.

658
00:25:41,912 --> 00:25:43,714
WE'VE BEEN TOGETHER
FOR THREE AND A HALF YEARS.

659
00:25:43,714 --> 00:25:46,083
WE DIDN'T KNOW I WAS PREGNANT
UNTIL I WAS FIVE MONTHS.

660
00:25:46,083 --> 00:25:48,518
I HAVE ENDOMETRIOSIS,
REALLY SEVERELY.

661
00:25:48,518 --> 00:25:50,354
I MEAN, I'M NOT SUPPOSED
TO BE ABLE TO HAVE KIDS.

662
00:25:50,354 --> 00:25:53,090
ENDOMETRIOSIS HAS TO DO
WITH YOUR REPRODUCTIVE SYSTEM,

663
00:25:53,090 --> 00:25:54,358
AND IT'S NOT CURABLE.

664
00:25:54,358 --> 00:25:55,492
IT'S SOMETHING THAT
YOU'RE BORN WITH.

665
00:25:55,492 --> 00:25:56,994
IT'S NOT SOMETHING
THAT YOU HAVE CONTROL OVER.

666
00:25:56,994 --> 00:25:58,228
IT IS VERY PAINFUL.

667
00:25:58,228 --> 00:26:01,498
I GAVE BIRTH,
AND HE CHANGED MY LIFE.

668
00:26:01,498 --> 00:26:03,700
HE IS MY MIRACLE BABY.
I MEAN, I HAVE A KID.

669
00:26:03,700 --> 00:26:04,935
I'M NOT SUPPOSED
TO BE ABLE TO.

670
00:26:04,935 --> 00:26:07,104
I'VE GAINED A SENSE
OF SELF-CONFIDENCE

671
00:26:07,104 --> 00:26:09,172
AND A FEELING OF SELF-WORTH
THAT IS JUST--

672
00:26:09,172 --> 00:26:11,275
- YOU CAN'T REPLACE IT.
- THANK YOU VERY MUCH.

673
00:26:12,509 --> 00:26:14,311
♪♪♪

674
00:26:14,311 --> 00:26:16,546
NOW THAT WE'VE MET
EACH GIRL INDIVIDUALLY,

675
00:26:16,546 --> 00:26:17,748
WE WANTED TO COMPARE THEM

676
00:26:17,748 --> 00:26:20,350
NEXT TO EACH OTHER
IN A LINGERIE WALK OFF

677
00:26:20,350 --> 00:26:22,586
TO SEE IF THEY COULD
SERVE IT.

678
00:26:22,586 --> 00:26:24,021
ALL RIGHTY,
IT'S A WALK-OFF,

679
00:26:24,021 --> 00:26:26,823
YOUR LAST CHANCE FOR
YOUR LAST IMPRESSION.

680
00:26:26,823 --> 00:26:28,025
FIERCE! WORK IT!

681
00:26:28,025 --> 00:26:29,493
♪ YOU GOTTA ROCK TO
THE RHYTHM WITH 'EM ♪

682
00:26:29,493 --> 00:26:30,761
♪ GOT TO GIVE IT TO 'EM ♪

683
00:26:30,761 --> 00:26:31,828
♪ GOT TO GIVE
A LOT MORE... ♪

684
00:26:31,828 --> 00:26:33,163
- HIT IT.
- ♪ THAN THE MINIMUM ♪

685
00:26:33,163 --> 00:26:34,531
♪ RAP TO THE RHYTHM
WITH 'EM ♪

686
00:26:34,531 --> 00:26:35,899
♪ GOT TO GIVE IT TO 'EM ♪

687
00:26:35,899 --> 00:26:37,668
- ♪ GOT TO GIVE A LOT MORE... ♪
- FIERCE!

688
00:26:37,668 --> 00:26:39,503
- GO.
- ♪ ROCK TO THE RHYTHM
WITH 'EM ♪

689
00:26:39,503 --> 00:26:40,671
♪ GOT TO GIVE IT TO 'EM ♪

690
00:26:40,671 --> 00:26:43,073
♪ GOT TO GIVE A LOT MORE
THAN THE MINIMUM... ♪

691
00:26:43,073 --> 00:26:44,308
♪ ROCK TO THE RHYTHM
WITH 'EM ♪

692
00:26:44,308 --> 00:26:45,776
♪ GOT TO GIVE IT TO 'EM ♪

693
00:26:45,776 --> 00:26:47,811
♪ GOT TO GIVE A LOT MORE ♪♪

694
00:26:49,246 --> 00:26:51,748
SO HOW WAS THIS
WHOLE PROCESS?

695
00:26:51,748 --> 00:26:53,216
FINE.

696
00:26:53,216 --> 00:26:55,652
SCARY?
NERVE-RACKING?

697
00:26:55,652 --> 00:26:57,387
THIS IS THE KIND OF SCARY
THAT CAN CHANGE YOUR LIVES.

698
00:26:57,387 --> 00:26:59,156
THAT'S RIGHT.

699
00:26:59,156 --> 00:27:02,426
- SO BYE-BYE.
- BYE-BYE.

700
00:27:02,426 --> 00:27:06,396
♪♪♪

701
00:27:08,131 --> 00:27:10,167
(applause)

702
00:27:10,167 --> 00:27:11,668
YOU GUYS BEEN HAVING FUN?

703
00:27:11,668 --> 00:27:14,071
YES!

704
00:27:14,071 --> 00:27:16,373
YEAH, BUT WE KNOW WHAT
I HAVE TO SAY, RIGHT?

705
00:27:16,373 --> 00:27:17,674
YEAH.

706
00:27:17,674 --> 00:27:21,111
TOMORROW MORNING, WE'RE HAVING
OUR BIG ELIMINATION.

707
00:27:21,111 --> 00:27:22,379
FIRST THING IN THE MORNING,

708
00:27:22,379 --> 00:27:24,715
ALARGE PORTION OF YOU GIRLS
ARE GONNA HAVE TO GO HOME.

709
00:27:24,715 --> 00:27:27,317
UNFORTUNATELY, I GOT TO
LEAVE YOU WITH THAT TONIGHT.

710
00:27:27,317 --> 00:27:28,452
GOOD LUCK TO ALL OF YOU,
THOUGH.

711
00:27:31,822 --> 00:27:33,690
I DO HAVE THAT
NERVOUSNESS INSIDE OF ME

712
00:27:33,690 --> 00:27:35,392
THAT HOPES THAT
I'M NOT GOING HOME.

713
00:27:35,392 --> 00:27:36,393
THANK YOU, JESUS.

714
00:27:36,393 --> 00:27:38,595
WE ASK YOU TO COME
INTO OUR CAREERS, GOD.

715
00:27:38,595 --> 00:27:41,064
THIS IS MY DREAM,
BUT AT THE SAME TIME,

716
00:27:41,064 --> 00:27:43,100
I BELIEVE WHAT GOD
HAS FOR ME IS FOR ME.

717
00:27:43,100 --> 00:27:45,502
SO IF THIS IS FOR ME,
I'M GONNA GET IT.

718
00:27:45,502 --> 00:27:46,737
AMEN.

719
00:27:49,373 --> 00:27:51,641
GOD, I AM SO NERVOUS.

720
00:27:51,641 --> 00:27:53,643
I AM PETRIFIED.

721
00:27:53,643 --> 00:27:56,012
OH. IT'S OKAY.

722
00:27:56,012 --> 00:27:58,315
WE WERE ALL IN THERE CRYING
LIKE WE WAS ON "OPRAH."

723
00:27:58,315 --> 00:28:00,550
HEY, YOU GUYS,
ALL THAT MAKEUP IS GONE.

724
00:28:01,885 --> 00:28:03,820
Y'ALL ARE SOME UGLY BITCHES.

725
00:28:03,820 --> 00:28:06,356
IT'D BE HARD GETTING CUT.

726
00:28:06,356 --> 00:28:07,858
WELL, THEM GETTIN' CUT.

727
00:28:07,858 --> 00:28:09,760
IT'S GONNA BE HARD.

728
00:28:09,760 --> 00:28:12,662
♪♪♪

729
00:28:17,300 --> 00:28:19,002
I DON'T KNOW HOW MANY
THEY'RE GOING TO CUT NOW.

730
00:28:19,002 --> 00:28:21,138
HOPEFULLY I'M NOT
ONE OF THEM.

731
00:28:21,138 --> 00:28:23,473
WE NOW HAVE
TO DO OUR FIRST CUT.

732
00:28:23,473 --> 00:28:26,276
AND WE'RE GONNA GO DOWN
FROM 35 TO...

733
00:28:26,276 --> 00:28:28,412
20.

734
00:28:28,412 --> 00:28:29,579
IN THE ROOM BEHIND ME,

735
00:28:29,579 --> 00:28:33,650
THERE ARE 20 PORTFOLIOS
ON THE TABLE.

736
00:28:33,650 --> 00:28:36,686
EACH PORTFOLIO HAS A PHOTOGRAPH
OF ONE GIRL INSIDE,

737
00:28:36,686 --> 00:28:41,091
AND THOSE PHOTOGRAPHS
REPRESENT THE 20 WOMEN

738
00:28:41,091 --> 00:28:44,628
THAT WILL BE MOVING ON TO
THE NEXT LEVEL OF COMPETITION

739
00:28:44,628 --> 00:28:45,996
ON "AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL."

740
00:28:47,798 --> 00:28:49,433
I'VE NEVER HAD TO GO
THROUGH ANYTHING LIKE THIS.

741
00:28:49,433 --> 00:28:52,135
IT'S THE MOST NERVOUS
I EVER HAVE BEEN.

742
00:28:52,135 --> 00:28:53,670
ARE YOU READY?

743
00:28:53,670 --> 00:28:55,739
(screaming)

744
00:28:55,739 --> 00:28:58,442
(both)
ONE, TWO, THREE.

745
00:28:59,776 --> 00:29:02,012
(all taking at once)

746
00:29:03,113 --> 00:29:04,414
SOON AS YOU WALK IN
THAT ROOM,

747
00:29:04,414 --> 00:29:06,550
DOUBT FREAKIN' KNOCKS YOU
RIGHT IN THE BACK OF THE HEAD.

748
00:29:06,550 --> 00:29:08,452
YOU KNOW, REALLY,
AM I GONNA TO MAKE THIS?

749
00:29:10,387 --> 00:29:11,555
YES!

750
00:29:16,960 --> 00:29:18,562
OH, THANK YOU SO MUCH!

751
00:29:18,562 --> 00:29:20,230
LIFE IS LOOKING UP.

752
00:29:20,230 --> 00:29:22,299
I GOT A PORTFOLIO,
SO I'M LOVING IT RIGHT NOW.

753
00:29:23,834 --> 00:29:25,202
I GOT ONE.

754
00:29:29,172 --> 00:29:30,907
MICHELLE.
WHERE ARE YOU, MICHELLE?

755
00:29:30,907 --> 00:29:34,244
OH, HELL YEAH!

756
00:29:34,244 --> 00:29:37,614
I AM FEELING TOTAL TEARS
OF JOY RIGHT NOW.

757
00:29:37,614 --> 00:29:40,050
THEY DIDN'T PICK
ANY OTHER PLUS SIZE GIRLS

758
00:29:40,050 --> 00:29:41,418
FOR ME
TO EVEN COMPETE WITH.

759
00:29:41,418 --> 00:29:45,222
I CAN BE AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP PLUS SIZE MODEL.

760
00:29:46,823 --> 00:29:49,759
I WASN'T CRYING
WHEN I SAW MY BOOK.

761
00:29:49,759 --> 00:29:52,796
BUT I CRIED WHEN I SAW THEM
NOT HAVING A BOOK.

762
00:29:56,433 --> 00:30:00,136
AND JUST TO SEE THESE GIRLS,
IT'S SO HARD.

763
00:30:00,136 --> 00:30:01,171
IT'S SO HARD.

764
00:30:04,040 --> 00:30:05,709
I DIDN'T MAKE THE CUT.

765
00:30:05,709 --> 00:30:10,146
SOMETHING SO BIG THAT
YOU'VE WANTED FOR SO LONG.

766
00:30:10,146 --> 00:30:12,182
AND IT'S OFFICIALLY
OVER NOW.

767
00:30:14,818 --> 00:30:15,886
STOP CRYING.

768
00:30:15,886 --> 00:30:17,320
CRYING IS FOR LOSERS.

769
00:30:17,320 --> 00:30:19,356
I FEEL GREAT
'CAUSE I AM STILL LIVIN'.

770
00:30:19,356 --> 00:30:21,458
I HAVE NINE LIVES.
RAWR.

771
00:30:21,458 --> 00:30:22,792
I WILL WIN THIS SUCKER.

772
00:30:25,161 --> 00:30:28,632
BEING ABLE TO BE HERE
AND ACTUALLY SEE THE DREAM

773
00:30:28,632 --> 00:30:32,435
IN THE PROCESS OF COMING TRUE
IS SO AMAZING.

774
00:30:32,435 --> 00:30:35,171
HOLLA BACK. IT WORKED.

775
00:30:35,171 --> 00:30:37,574
ALL OF THE GIRLS
ARE INCREDIBLE.

776
00:30:37,574 --> 00:30:39,042
I'M SERIOUSLY IMPRESSED.

777
00:30:39,042 --> 00:30:40,677
I DON'T KNOW HOW THEY'RE
GONNA NARROW IT DOWN.

778
00:30:40,677 --> 00:30:42,746
THE COMPETITION, YOU KNOW,
IT'S A LITTLE HARDER NOW

779
00:30:42,746 --> 00:30:44,648
SO I KNOW I HAVE TO
PUT MY BEST FOOT FORWARD.

780
00:30:44,648 --> 00:30:47,717
I WENT TOO FAR WITH THIS
TO GO BACK.

781
00:30:47,717 --> 00:30:49,319
WHO WILL MAKE
THE FINAL 14?

782
00:30:49,319 --> 00:30:52,556
DON'T GO AWAY-- THERE'S MORE
"TOP MODEL" COMING UP.

783
00:30:59,696 --> 00:31:03,633
♪♪♪

784
00:31:03,633 --> 00:31:05,168
THE REMAINING 20 GIRLS

785
00:31:05,168 --> 00:31:07,037
WALKED DOWNSTAIRS
AFTER THE FIRST CUT,

786
00:31:07,037 --> 00:31:08,772
AND WE WALKED INTO A ROOM.

787
00:31:10,340 --> 00:31:12,475
THIS IS YOUR FIRST
PICTURE ASSIGNMENT,

788
00:31:12,475 --> 00:31:14,911
SO GET IN THE PHOTO BOOTH
AND TAKE YOUR OWN PICTURES.

789
00:31:14,911 --> 00:31:16,613
I'M TRYING TO THINK OF
FOUR DIFFERENT POSES TO DO.

790
00:31:16,613 --> 00:31:18,949
- I KNOW. ME TOO.
- I CAN THINK OF ONE.

791
00:31:18,949 --> 00:31:21,051
I DEFINITELY THINK THE JUDGES
ARE LOOKING FOR, YOU KNOW,

792
00:31:21,051 --> 00:31:22,118
US TO GET
IN THIS PHOTO BOOTH

793
00:31:22,118 --> 00:31:23,753
AND BASICALLY JUST SHOW
OUR PERSONALITY.

794
00:31:23,753 --> 00:31:25,055
FLUTTER YOUR EYELASHES.

795
00:31:26,690 --> 00:31:28,525
I'M NOT NERVOUS
ABOUT THE PHOTO SHOOT.

796
00:31:28,525 --> 00:31:31,261
JUST NERVOUS 'CAUSE I KNOW
THEY'RE GOING TO BE JUDGING IT.

797
00:31:31,261 --> 00:31:35,165
♪♪♪

798
00:31:42,205 --> 00:31:44,107
OH, THIS IS NOT WORKING.

799
00:31:44,107 --> 00:31:46,409
I WAS, LIKE, TRYING
TO CATCH THE CAMERA.

800
00:31:47,877 --> 00:31:49,579
THEN I'M LIKE,
I'M LIKE, YOU KNOW WHAT?

801
00:31:49,579 --> 00:31:50,914
FORGET IT. I'M JUST GONNA
LOOK AT THE CAMERA,

802
00:31:50,914 --> 00:31:53,416
SO MY PICTURES
CAME OUT PRETTY MESSED UP.

803
00:31:53,416 --> 00:31:54,851
SCREW THIS THING.

804
00:31:54,851 --> 00:31:57,887
THAT WAS, LIKE, THE FIRST
OPPORTUNITY TO SIZE UP

805
00:31:57,887 --> 00:31:59,456
THE REST OF MY COMPETITION,

806
00:31:59,456 --> 00:32:03,460
AND I TOTALLY WANTED
TO GIVE SOMETHING DYNAMIC.

807
00:32:05,195 --> 00:32:07,330
THAT'S IT.

808
00:32:07,330 --> 00:32:08,632
I AM GONNA BE MYSELF.

809
00:32:08,632 --> 00:32:10,867
YOU KNOW, IF YOU LEARN THINGS
FROM OTHER GIRLS,

810
00:32:10,867 --> 00:32:13,036
CERTAIN POSES
AND CERTAIN VOGUES...

811
00:32:13,036 --> 00:32:15,271
WOW, THAT LOOKS GOOD.
LET'S TRY IT OUT ON ME.

812
00:32:15,271 --> 00:32:17,040
ESTELA.

813
00:32:17,040 --> 00:32:20,243
♪♪♪

814
00:32:23,446 --> 00:32:24,948
THIS LITTLE MACHINE
TAKES GOOD PICTURES.

815
00:32:24,948 --> 00:32:25,949
YEAH.

816
00:32:27,984 --> 00:32:30,320
HELLO, MY FIERCE MR. JAY,
MISS J.

817
00:32:30,320 --> 00:32:32,756
- MISS T.
- HEY.

818
00:32:32,756 --> 00:32:34,858
WE HAVE 20 GIRLS HERE.

819
00:32:34,858 --> 00:32:37,060
WE HAVE TO NARROW IT DOWN
TO 14,

820
00:32:37,060 --> 00:32:38,962
AND THEY'LL BE
MOVING INTO THE HOUSE.

821
00:32:38,962 --> 00:32:40,030
OKAY, SO KEENYAH.

822
00:32:40,030 --> 00:32:41,665
KEENYAH--
SHE WAS A LITTLE FLAT.

823
00:32:41,665 --> 00:32:43,867
YOU DON'T NEED EVERYBODY
TO BE CRAZY.

824
00:32:43,867 --> 00:32:45,869
I AM NOT CRAZY.

825
00:32:45,869 --> 00:32:48,071
ALL RIGHT. TATIANA.

826
00:32:48,071 --> 00:32:49,973
SHE MAY GET A LITTLE ROUGH
AROUND THE EDGES.

827
00:32:49,973 --> 00:32:53,443
ANY GIRL THAT CAN LOOK
THIS FIERCE IN A PHOTO BOOTH

828
00:32:53,443 --> 00:32:55,145
IS WORTH TAKING
A SECOND LOOK AT.

829
00:32:55,145 --> 00:32:56,312
JENNIFER B.

830
00:32:56,312 --> 00:32:58,248
I LOVE A GIRL THAT HAS
A HORRIBLE RUNWAY WALK,

831
00:32:58,248 --> 00:32:59,783
BECAUSE IT GIVES YOU
SO MUCH TO WORK WITH.

832
00:32:59,783 --> 00:33:00,784
KAHLEN.

833
00:33:00,784 --> 00:33:02,519
THERE'S SOMETHING
I LIKE ABOUT A GIRL

834
00:33:02,519 --> 00:33:04,788
WHO DOESN'T KNOW
WHAT SHE'S DOING

835
00:33:04,788 --> 00:33:07,190
BECAUSE THAT MEANS
THERE'S THE POTENTIAL

836
00:33:07,190 --> 00:33:08,324
TO REALLY TEACH HER
SOMETHING.

837
00:33:08,324 --> 00:33:09,325
LLUVY.

838
00:33:09,325 --> 00:33:11,795
I LOVE THE SHELLEY DUVALL,
LIZA MINNELLI THING

839
00:33:11,795 --> 00:33:12,796
GOING ON HERE IN THE EYES.

840
00:33:12,796 --> 00:33:13,863
- GIRAFFE LASHES.
- YES.

841
00:33:13,863 --> 00:33:15,498
SHE'S A LITTLE PEAR-SHAPED.

842
00:33:15,498 --> 00:33:17,267
NOELLE--
I THINK THAT GIRL POPS.

843
00:33:17,267 --> 00:33:20,070
THE BRIGHTNESS AND THE SHINE
THAT COMES FROM WITHIN,

844
00:33:20,070 --> 00:33:22,205
IT MAKES ME WANT
TO SEE HER IN PICTURES.

845
00:33:22,205 --> 00:33:23,406
BUT, TYRA, CAN I SAY NO?

846
00:33:23,406 --> 00:33:25,809
- NO.
- OOH!

847
00:33:25,809 --> 00:33:26,876
BRITTANY.

848
00:33:26,876 --> 00:33:29,179
BRITTANY LOOKS EXACTLY
LIKE JANICE DICKINSON.

849
00:33:29,179 --> 00:33:31,114
NAIMA--SHE'S SO EDGY.

850
00:33:31,114 --> 00:33:32,315
SHE'S JUST, LIKE, MM!

851
00:33:32,315 --> 00:33:34,284
EDGY IS ONE THING,
BUT CAN WE TAKE HER FURTHER?

852
00:33:34,284 --> 00:33:36,920
- MICHELLE D.
- YOU KNOW HOW I FEEL
ABOUT NO-NECK MONSTERS.

853
00:33:36,920 --> 00:33:38,354
SHE'S GOT A NECK,
SHE JUST DOESN'T KNOW

854
00:33:38,354 --> 00:33:40,223
HOW TO CARRY HERSELF
IN A ROOM YET.

855
00:33:40,223 --> 00:33:41,524
BRANDY.

856
00:33:41,524 --> 00:33:42,525
DO YOU KNOW
WHAT I DON'T LIKE?

857
00:33:42,525 --> 00:33:44,194
THE WEAVE HER MOM
DID FOR HER.

858
00:33:44,194 --> 00:33:47,464
I LOVE BRANDY'S HAIR.
IN FACT, SHE'S FIERCE.

859
00:33:47,464 --> 00:33:48,465
LINDSEY.

860
00:33:48,465 --> 00:33:49,999
SHE'S A MODEL
FROM HERE DOWN.

861
00:33:49,999 --> 00:33:52,168
AND MARIE OSMOND
FROM THERE UP.

862
00:33:52,168 --> 00:33:54,104
- BRITA.
- I THINK SHE'S BEAUTIFUL

863
00:33:54,104 --> 00:33:57,006
AND EVERYTHING IS GOING
SO GLAMOROUS IN FASHION,

864
00:33:57,006 --> 00:33:58,608
SHE COULD LEND HERSELF
WELL TO THAT.

865
00:33:58,608 --> 00:34:00,076
OKAY. SARAH.

866
00:34:00,076 --> 00:34:01,544
I LOVE THIS GIRL'S FACE.

867
00:34:01,544 --> 00:34:02,645
SHE CAN GIVE YOU
SOMETHING.

868
00:34:02,645 --> 00:34:03,680
ESTELA.

869
00:34:03,680 --> 00:34:05,448
JUST BECAUSE OF HER STORY,

870
00:34:05,448 --> 00:34:07,350
I WANT TO HAVE HER
ON BOARD.

871
00:34:07,350 --> 00:34:10,186
BUT THAT'S NOT A REASON TO
BRING A MODEL INTO THE HOUSE.

872
00:34:10,186 --> 00:34:12,322
THERE IS SO MUCH DEADLY
WALK IN THAT GIRL.

873
00:34:12,322 --> 00:34:14,124
I THINK SHE HAS
SOMETHING TO OFFER.

874
00:34:14,124 --> 00:34:15,291
REBECCA.

875
00:34:15,291 --> 00:34:16,760
I THINK SHE'S
A CLEAN PALATE.

876
00:34:16,760 --> 00:34:19,395
SHE'S GOT THAT LITTLE
SHORT SIMPLE BLOND HAIR.

877
00:34:19,395 --> 00:34:21,397
BUT REBECCA'S A LITTLE
ACTRESS LOOKING,

878
00:34:21,397 --> 00:34:24,133
AND THAT MIGHT
NOT WORK FOR HER.

879
00:34:24,133 --> 00:34:25,301
LADY KAT.

880
00:34:25,301 --> 00:34:27,203
- I LOVE LADY KAT'S BODY...
- YEAH.

881
00:34:27,203 --> 00:34:29,004
AND I DO LOVE HER FACE.

882
00:34:29,004 --> 00:34:30,173
TIFFANY.

883
00:34:30,173 --> 00:34:31,374
THERE'S SOMETHING
ABOUT TIFFANY

884
00:34:31,374 --> 00:34:34,477
THAT I FEEL THAT WE CAN BUILD
AND MAKE HER MORE VERSATILE.

885
00:34:34,477 --> 00:34:36,780
I THINK LADY KAT IS GONNA
GIVE US ONE THING.

886
00:34:36,780 --> 00:34:39,149
ONE, TWO, THREE.
RAWR.

887
00:34:39,149 --> 00:34:41,283
MARY. LOOK AT THAT COMMERCIAL
LITTLE SHOT OF HER.

888
00:34:41,283 --> 00:34:44,521
LOOK AT THIS TOP SHOT.
SHE LOOKS SO BEAUTIFUL.

889
00:34:44,521 --> 00:34:45,988
YEAH, BUT I DON'T THINK
IT IS FAIR, TYRA,

890
00:34:45,988 --> 00:34:49,024
WHEN YOU PUT ONE GIRL
TO COMPETE WITH OTHER GIRLS

891
00:34:49,024 --> 00:34:50,627
- THAT ARE NOT THE SAME SIZE.
- MM-HMM.

892
00:34:50,627 --> 00:34:54,164
EVERYBODY HAS THEIR FAVORITES,
BUT SIX GIRLS HAVE TO GO HOME.

893
00:34:54,164 --> 00:34:57,167
♪♪♪

894
00:34:57,167 --> 00:34:58,635
GOD, I DON'T THINK I HAVE

895
00:34:58,635 --> 00:35:00,570
EVER WANTED THIS MORE
IN MY LIFE.

896
00:35:00,570 --> 00:35:04,007
I FEEL IT WITH ALL
OF MY HEART AND MY SOUL.

897
00:35:04,007 --> 00:35:05,809
IF I WERE TO
WIN THIS COMPETITION,

898
00:35:05,809 --> 00:35:07,210
IT WOULD CHANGE
EVERYTHING.

899
00:35:07,210 --> 00:35:10,613
ME AND MY DAUGHTER--
IT WOULD JUST BE A BLESSING.

900
00:35:10,613 --> 00:35:12,715
A BLESSING.

901
00:35:12,715 --> 00:35:14,217
I'M SO HAPPY TO BE HERE.

902
00:35:14,217 --> 00:35:15,251
IT'S JUST SO MUCH.

903
00:35:15,251 --> 00:35:16,252
IT'S OVERWHELMING,

904
00:35:16,252 --> 00:35:19,255
AND I'M JUST USED TO
FAILING AT EVERYTHING.

905
00:35:19,255 --> 00:35:21,391
BACK HOME, EVEN THOUGH
MY GRANDMOTHER LOVED ME,

906
00:35:21,391 --> 00:35:24,694
IT'S A DOUBT IN THEIR MIND
THAT TIFFANY MIGHT NOT DO IT.

907
00:35:26,729 --> 00:35:30,633
♪♪♪

908
00:35:37,674 --> 00:35:40,844
- HI, LADIES.
- HI.

909
00:35:40,844 --> 00:35:43,580
THIS IS
THE FINAL ELIMINATION.

910
00:35:43,580 --> 00:35:47,784
THOUSANDS UPON THOUSANDS
OF GIRLS WAITED IN THOSE LINES

911
00:35:47,784 --> 00:35:49,719
THAT YOU ALL WAITED IN
FOR HOURS AND HOURS,

912
00:35:49,719 --> 00:35:52,121
BUT THEY'RE NOT HERE.

913
00:35:52,121 --> 00:35:53,990
YOU ALL ARE HERE.

914
00:35:53,990 --> 00:35:55,191
AND THAT MAKES YOU
EXTRA SPECIAL.

915
00:35:55,191 --> 00:35:58,461
AND I CHOSE EVERY
SINGLE ONE OF YOU TO BE HERE.

916
00:35:58,461 --> 00:36:04,033
14 GIRLS TONIGHT WILL BE
IN THE RUNNING

917
00:36:04,033 --> 00:36:07,770
TOWARDS BECOMING
AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL.

918
00:36:07,770 --> 00:36:10,707
THE FIRST NAME THAT
I'M GOING TO CALL...

919
00:36:17,680 --> 00:36:18,681
REBECCA.

920
00:36:23,553 --> 00:36:25,121
CHRISTINA.

921
00:36:28,758 --> 00:36:29,993
KEENYAH.

922
00:36:35,465 --> 00:36:37,233
THE NEXT NAME...

923
00:36:39,869 --> 00:36:41,237
BRITA.

924
00:36:45,775 --> 00:36:48,077
NAIMA.

925
00:36:48,077 --> 00:36:49,145
OH, MY GOD.

926
00:36:52,615 --> 00:36:54,751
- THANK YOU.
- YOU'RE WELCOME.

927
00:36:59,155 --> 00:37:00,390
NOELLE.

928
00:37:02,358 --> 00:37:04,961
OH, MY GOD.

929
00:37:04,961 --> 00:37:06,663
THE SEVENTH NAME...

930
00:37:10,500 --> 00:37:11,501
MICHELLE.

931
00:37:11,501 --> 00:37:13,770
OH, YES!

932
00:37:13,770 --> 00:37:16,639
OH, YEAH! YEAH!

933
00:37:19,575 --> 00:37:20,743
SARAH.

934
00:37:22,111 --> 00:37:23,079
OH, MY GOD.

935
00:37:27,550 --> 00:37:33,389
BRANDY.

936
00:37:33,389 --> 00:37:34,557
(cries)

937
00:37:34,557 --> 00:37:37,093
BRANDY.

938
00:37:37,093 --> 00:37:38,594
HOW DO YOU FEEL,
BRANDY?

939
00:37:38,594 --> 00:37:43,199
I JUST THANK GOD FOR BEING
IN THIS LINE RIGHT NOW.

940
00:37:44,934 --> 00:37:48,338
THE NEXT NAME
THAT I AM GOING TO CALL...

941
00:37:50,039 --> 00:37:52,842
- BRITTANY!
- OH, MY GOD!

942
00:37:52,842 --> 00:37:54,711
YES! I WAS WAITING
FOR MY NAME!

943
00:37:54,711 --> 00:37:56,212
YEAH, YEAH!

944
00:37:56,212 --> 00:37:58,014
OH, MY GOD.

945
00:37:58,014 --> 00:37:59,682
I WAS GETTIN' SO SCARED.

946
00:37:59,682 --> 00:38:03,152
OH, MY GOD. OH, MY GOD.
OH, MY GOD.

947
00:38:07,690 --> 00:38:08,925
KAHLEN.

948
00:38:11,961 --> 00:38:13,162
HOLD ON. WHAT?

949
00:38:13,162 --> 00:38:14,897
KAHLEN.

950
00:38:14,897 --> 00:38:16,532
YOU HEARD HER RIGHT.

951
00:38:19,936 --> 00:38:21,838
I JUST DIDN'T BREATHE
FOR TEN MINUTES STRAIGHT.

952
00:38:21,838 --> 00:38:23,639
(laughter)

953
00:38:25,508 --> 00:38:28,378
I HAVE THREE NAMES LEFT.

954
00:38:32,882 --> 00:38:34,884
THE NEXT NAME THAT I AM
GOING TO CALL--

955
00:38:36,252 --> 00:38:37,754
TATIANA.

956
00:38:40,957 --> 00:38:42,425
COME HERE.

957
00:38:48,498 --> 00:38:49,799
LLUVY.

958
00:38:58,307 --> 00:39:01,978
I HAVE SEVEN BEAUTIFUL GIRLS
STANDING BEFORE ME...

959
00:39:04,414 --> 00:39:08,918
SEVEN BEAUTIFUL GIRLS THAT CAME
FROM ALL ACROSS THIS COUNTRY...

960
00:39:10,486 --> 00:39:13,423
SEVEN BEAUTIFUL GIRLS THAT
ARE BEAUTIFUL ON THE INSIDE

961
00:39:13,423 --> 00:39:16,192
AS WELL AS THE OUTSIDE.

962
00:39:16,192 --> 00:39:19,429
BUT I ONLY HAVE
ONE NAME LEFT.

963
00:39:19,429 --> 00:39:23,066
THE LAST NAME THAT I CALL

964
00:39:23,066 --> 00:39:27,070
WILL COMPLETE THIS GROUP
OVER HERE

965
00:39:27,070 --> 00:39:29,639
AND WILL BE
THE 14th FINALIST.

966
00:39:32,842 --> 00:39:35,144
THE LAST NAME THAT
I'M GOING TO CALL...

967
00:39:41,350 --> 00:39:42,351
TIFFANY.

968
00:39:42,351 --> 00:39:45,655
(cheering)

969
00:39:45,655 --> 00:39:47,557
TIFFANY, YES!

970
00:39:48,724 --> 00:39:50,293
OH, MY HEART.

971
00:39:50,293 --> 00:39:51,394
DON'T CRY, GIRL.

972
00:39:51,394 --> 00:39:54,831
- YES! YES!
- WHOO!

973
00:40:02,738 --> 00:40:05,007
GRANDMA, I'M GOIN' ON.

974
00:40:08,778 --> 00:40:10,947
- I'M GLAD SHE MADE IT.
- OH, DON'T CRY, HONEY.

975
00:40:10,947 --> 00:40:13,983
NO, I'M HAPPY FOR HER.
I WANT HER TO HAVE IT.

976
00:40:30,366 --> 00:40:31,501
I'M REALLY DISAPPOINTED.

977
00:40:31,501 --> 00:40:33,703
I JUST FEEL LIKE
MY HEART'S BROKEN.

978
00:40:33,703 --> 00:40:38,274
I FEEL LIKE I'VE--I'VE--
I'VE COME SO FAR

979
00:40:38,274 --> 00:40:41,177
AND TO MAKE IT THIS FAR
AND BE SHUT DOWN TWICE,

980
00:40:41,177 --> 00:40:44,180
I JUST-- I JUST
DON'T UNDERSTAND.

981
00:41:01,097 --> 00:41:03,399
OKAY?
ALL RIGHT, HONEY.

982
00:41:08,838 --> 00:41:10,306
THIS WAS GONNA BE
A TRANSFORMATION

983
00:41:10,306 --> 00:41:13,509
FOR THE POSITIVE
FOR ME AND MY DAUGHTER,

984
00:41:13,509 --> 00:41:16,112
BUT REGARDLESS OF THE FACT,
WE WILL COME OUT ON TOP.

985
00:41:16,112 --> 00:41:19,148
SO I WISH
ALL THE LADIES LUCK.

986
00:41:19,148 --> 00:41:20,816
DREAMS CAN'T BE THIS GOOD.

987
00:41:20,816 --> 00:41:22,652
THEY'VE NEVER FELT
THIS GOOD BEFORE.

988
00:41:22,652 --> 00:41:24,086
I MADE IT. YES.

989
00:41:24,086 --> 00:41:26,789
I AM SORRY, HONEY.
YES!

990
00:41:26,789 --> 00:41:29,525
OH, MY GRANDMA
GON' BE SO HAPPY.

991
00:41:29,525 --> 00:41:31,093
I WENT FROM
AMERICA'S MOST WANTED

992
00:41:31,093 --> 00:41:33,462
TO AMERICA'S NEXT
TOP MODEL.

993
00:41:33,462 --> 00:41:35,331
I'M SO HAPPY.
I'M JUST HAPPY.

994
00:41:35,331 --> 00:41:39,035
CHILD, MY GRANDMA--
GRANDMA...

995
00:41:40,169 --> 00:41:44,073
♪♪♪

996
00:41:56,152 --> 00:42:01,591
STAY TUNED FOR SCENES
FROM OUR NEXT EPISODE.

997
00:42:01,591 --> 00:42:04,961
COMING UP ON
"AMERICA'S NEXT TOP MODEL"...

998
00:42:04,961 --> 00:42:06,329
FASHION POLICE.

999
00:42:06,329 --> 00:42:09,298
FOR THEIR FIRST PHOTO SHOOT,
THE GIRLS ARE PUT TO THE TEST

1000
00:42:09,298 --> 00:42:11,300
BY THE BEST...

1001
00:42:11,300 --> 00:42:12,935
THERE'S PEOPLE
WALKING AROUND.

1002
00:42:12,935 --> 00:42:16,806
THE NEW NEIGHBORHOOD DOESN'T
MEET THEIR EXPECTATIONS...

1003
00:42:17,907 --> 00:42:20,276
BUT IT'S THEIR ATTITUDE
AT THE MAKEOVERS...

1004
00:42:20,276 --> 00:42:22,745
TWO OF YOU PISSED ME OFF.

1005
00:42:22,745 --> 00:42:24,614
THAT CROSSES THE LINE.

